1. Press **Replace** and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.
2. Or press **Remove**, then **Remove the photo**.

> Good to know: Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.

## Add several cars at once

Open **Cars**, then **Add cars from a VIN list**.

1. Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.
2. Press **Preview**: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.
3. Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press **Add**.

Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.

## Service and maintenance

On a car''s page, under Service and maintenance.

- What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.
- Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.
- You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.
- It is read only: call or message us about a service.

## Take new listing photos

Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.

1. On the car''s page, press **Add listing photos** (or **Take new photos** for a car already live).
2. Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot in the list. Press **Retake** if one is not right.
4. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
5. Press **Submit for listing**. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg "phone; size: 390 610; pins: 4 92.3 43.4, 3 76.9 70.2")

## Price limits

Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.

1. **Cars**, **Price limits for every car**, at the bottom: type a **Minimum a day** and a **Maximum a day** in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press **Save price limits**.
2. One car different? Open it: **Price limits** has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.
3. Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.

## Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** shows the car''s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, **Cars** > **Cars you referred** shows their cars'' bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.

## Studio photos (release 48)

- We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.
- Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.
- We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in **Account**, **Notifications**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Home tells you what to do next. Each car has its own page with its status, terms, bookings, invoices and photos.</p><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-home-at-a-glance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Home at a glance</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The menu: Home, Cars (your cars and their bookings), Money (statements, payouts and invoices), Documents and Account (profile, banking and notifications). Each of Cars, Money and Account is one page with a row of tabs on top. Home starts with the next thing to do, then one line with what you earned so far this month, how many cars are out, the next payout and any fees due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At the top: each car with its photo and its status right now (On rent, Available or In service), this month&#39;s rental charges against last month, the next payout and the days rented this month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your earnings: a column per month. Press a month, or the arrows, for its bookings, days rented, rental charges, fees billed and the payout on its statement. Choose a car to see it alone, or <b class="gd-ui">Payouts</b> for the statement amounts. Beside it, Money (what is due now, your fees each month, the next billing date and the next payout date) and Coming up, your next bookings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Your vehicles: each car with this month so far, its next booking and what it needs next. Got another car? Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a vehicle</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1270"><img src="/guides/img/owner-01-home-desktop-9035b084.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1270"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.1%;top:8.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:72.9%;top:30.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:31.2%;top:85%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>When something needs you (a signature, a payment or an upload), it is the first thing on Home.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-a-car-s-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s page</h2><p class="gd-p">Open Cars, then a car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The top shows the car&#39;s photo, its plate, how it is enrolled and its status right now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Terms: the Insurance Fee, the Revenue Share, your enrolment date and a link to the listing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">This car by month (choose a month with the arrows or its column), Coming up, and Bookings with every trip in your car. <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> reserves it for you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leaving explains the exit notice and has the button to give it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/vehicles/1f21c3e5-39c3-4d54-ae0d-cbb2512835e7</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1242"><img src="/guides/img/owner-03-vehicle-desktop-7f1a9a38.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1242"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:55.6%;top:25.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:38%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:36.5%;top:54.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.2%;top:67%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">While a car is being set up, its page also shows the <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding</b> checklist and the uploads it still needs: the ownership permit, the lender&#39;s permission and the insurance.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-where-your-car-is" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where your car is</h2><p class="gd-p">Once your car has its tracker, its page shows <b class="gd-ui">Where your car is</b>: moving or parked, when it last reported, and <b class="gd-ui">Open on the map</b>. Below it, the trips of the last 30 days: when, how far, and where each started and ended.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No tracker on the car yet? It says <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You see the location and the trips only. The renter&#39;s name and the booking stay private, as before.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-tracker-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker alerts</h2><p class="gd-p">Once your car has its tracker, its page shows <b class="gd-ui">Tracker alerts</b> below <b class="gd-ui">Where your car is</b>: what the tracker recorded in the last 30 days.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Speeding, harsh driving, the car outside Ontario, driving after the return time, the tracker unplugged or tampered with, or the car parked at an impound lot.</li><li>Leaving Ontario or leaving Canada: we tell you at once, and CarmaCars calls the renter.</li><li>Each alert says what happened and when, with <b class="gd-ui">See the place</b>.</li><li>We also tell you by email, text or the app when one happens.</li></ul><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> and the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing there? It says nothing was recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To stop these alerts or change how they reach you, open <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b> and turn <b class="gd-ui">Tracker alert on your car</b> off or on.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>There is nothing for you to do. CarmaCars handles each one with the renter and collects any charge with its evidence. You see the event and the place only, never the renter or the booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-the-onboarding-checklist" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The onboarding checklist</h2><p class="gd-p">Home and each car&#39;s page show the same <b class="gd-ui">Onboarding checklist</b>. Each step says one of four things: done, to do (and who it waits on: you, CarmaCars, or another office such as the registry), blocked (and why, for example &quot;First: terms approved&quot;), or not needed. A step that waits on you has one button: the one thing to do for it, such as <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Upload the ownership permit</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-change-an-onboarding-photo" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an onboarding photo</h2><p class="gd-p">A wrong ownership permit, insurance slip or lender&#39;s letter? Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Your onboarding photos</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> and choose the new photo or PDF. The new one is checked again by CarmaCars, even if the old one was approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove the photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is kept in our history. CarmaCars staff can replace or remove a photo for you too.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-add-several-cars-at-once" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add several cars at once</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Add cars from a VIN list</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the VINs (one a line), or upload a CSV or text file. Up to 50 at a time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b>: each VIN is read (year, make and model). A typo (the check digit does not match), a car already with us or one listed twice is shown and not added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Say for each car whether it is owned outright, financed or leased (with the lender), then press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Each car then waits for us to approve its terms, like any new car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-service-and-maintenance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Service and maintenance</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, under Service and maintenance.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>What is due on your car (oil change, tires, brakes, inspections, the registration) and the tires on it.</li><li>Every service we recorded: the date, the odometer, the shop, what was done and who paid.</li><li>You pay for maintenance and routine wear (your agreement, 11.1). A service we paid for shows its amount and is deducted on your next statement as an owner cost.</li><li>It is read only: call or message us about a service.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-take-new-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Take new listing photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Good photos get more bookings. You can shoot them yourself with your phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car&#39;s page, press <b class="gd-ui">Add listing photos</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Take new photos</b> for a car already live).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the tips for each shot: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot in the list. Press <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> if one is not right.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. New photos replace the current ones once our team approves them.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/610"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-d0b13740.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="610"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.3%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:70.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-price-limits" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Price limits</h2><p class="gd-p">Choose the lowest and the highest daily rate your cars are rented at.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Price limits for every car</b>, at the bottom: type a <b class="gd-ui">Minimum a day</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Maximum a day</b> in dollars, or leave one empty for no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One car different? Open it: <b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b> has the same two fields for that car only. Empty there, your limits for every car apply.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Short-notice and booked-ahead pricing, promo codes, discounts and our offers keep the rental a day between them; fees, add-ons and tax are not counted. Only a CarmaCars Admin can make an exception on one booking, and it is recorded.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-pickup-and-return-records-cars-you-referred-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup and return records, cars you referred (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> shows the car&#39;s condition when we picked it up from you and when we gave it back: the photos, km and fuel. If you referred another owner, <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> shows their cars&#39; bookings, use and revenue, read only, and your referral share is a line on your statements.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="home-and-your-vehicles-studio-photos-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio photos (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>We make studio photos of your car from its own photos, so every car on CarmaCars looks photographed the same way. The side profile is first.</li><li>Your own photos stay on the page, right after the studio photos. The page tells renters which ones are studio photos.</li><li>We email you when they are live. If the colour or wheels look wrong, reply and we make them again. You can turn this email off in <b class="gd-ui">Account</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Notifications</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'fleet-and-listings', 'chapter', 'calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms', 'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from **Find a car** (**Car map**) and field staff under **Map**, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car''s page and a booking''s page show **Where the car is** (or **No tracker yet**). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.
- Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as **Redo every car** on the Photo standard card.

## The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)

Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.

- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.
- **Missing angles.** Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car''s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked **AI generated** on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.
- **The order.** The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. **Redo this car now** makes all of its photos again at once; **Redo every car** makes every photo of every car again. **Redo photos with Gemini** on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; **Publish shifts** adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. **Missing check-in and check-out**, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with **Give to field staff**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car shows nine generated views: front three-quarter (always first), front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each one from references, so the car is the real car and the room looks like a real showroom.

- **What Gemini is sent.** The car''s own photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has fewer than three, or none of that side, its newest check-in and check-out photos as well (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only), the stock photo of the model, and for an outside view the showroom background plate. The words describe each angle: camera height, lens, crop, the car centred, 45 degrees for a three-quarter. Plates blurred, no text, no logos added.
- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site.
- **The real photos.** They stay in the car''s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked **AI generated** for staff only.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch for the generated views.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows each car''s **Generated set** (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and "from check-in photos" when those were used). **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car** make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.
- **Showroom background plates** (**Program settings**, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; **Make a new one** has Gemini make it again.

## The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)

Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.

- The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model''s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the scene for every car. On a car, **Studio photos** > **Scene** picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).
- No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car''s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.
- One set everywhere: once a car''s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car''s record.
- The check: Gemini checks each view against the car''s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.
- On a car, **Studio photos** shows each view beside the car''s own photos of that angle, marked **AI**. **Make again** makes one view again; **Take off the site** and **Put on the site**.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows the fleet''s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini''s daily limit.
- Marketing set: **Make the marketing set** uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked **AI**; tick **In the ZIP** for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.
- Background plates (**Program settings**, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.

## Studio renders first (release 48)

- Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.
- On the site the renders come first, in this order: side profile (the nose to the left, the cover), front three-quarter, front, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. The car''s own photos follow, on the same branded background. They are never hidden.
- A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.
- The car page says **Rendered photos** above the gallery, with **See its real photos**.
- New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model''s daily limit.
- When a car''s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert ("Your car has new studio photos"), and Fleet gets "Studio photos live" in the next digest. Look the photos over.
- The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in **Data health**: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.
', 'Fleet and listings', 'Vehicles, the listing pipeline, similar cars and covering licence plates.',
  'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from **Find a car** (**Car map**) and field staff under **Map**, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car''s page and a booking''s page show **Where the car is** (or **No tracker yet**). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)

Below the map on the **Fleet tracking** tab of **Cars**. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on **Tracker events** under **Tracker event settings**.

On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car''s owner:

- **Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h**: one record per event, at the highest limit reached, with that limit''s speeding charge of Settings > Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). One event is one charge: 226 km/h is $1,000, not $500 plus $1,000. The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).
- **Over the speeding alert level** (140 km/h) and **harsh driving**: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.
- **Left Ontario**, **driving after the return time**, a tracker unplugged or tampered with: a notice with the clause. No set charge.
- **Left Canada**: urgent, once per crossing. Admins and on-duty Fleet get an alert, an email and a text at once (always on), Fleet gets an urgent To do, and the renter is told that leaving Canada needs written approval (rental agreement 10.1). Leaving Ontario for another province or a state reaches the same people the same way.
- **Driving at night** (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.
- **At a pound**: see Pound flags below.

The **Tracker events** table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.

1. To bill a speeding record, press **Charge** on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.
2. The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.

**Pound flags**: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot''s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.

1. Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.
2. Press **Record the path**: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened.
3. A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.

**Pound lots**: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.

1. Press **Find the pins from the addresses** once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.
2. **Edit** a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick **I checked these details with the lot**.
3. **Add a lot** for any other pound you know of.

> Note: The renter''s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.
- Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as **Redo every car** on the Photo standard card.

## The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)

Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.

- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.
- **Missing angles.** Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car''s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked **AI generated** on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.
- **The order.** The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. **Redo this car now** makes all of its photos again at once; **Redo every car** makes every photo of every car again. **Redo photos with Gemini** on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; **Publish shifts** adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. **Missing check-in and check-out**, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with **Give to field staff**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car shows nine generated views: front three-quarter (always first), front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each one from references, so the car is the real car and the room looks like a real showroom.

- **What Gemini is sent.** The car''s own photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has fewer than three, or none of that side, its newest check-in and check-out photos as well (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only), the stock photo of the model, and for an outside view the showroom background plate. The words describe each angle: camera height, lens, crop, the car centred, 45 degrees for a three-quarter. Plates blurred, no text, no logos added.
- **The check.** A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site.
- **The real photos.** They stay in the car''s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked **AI generated** for staff only.
- **By itself.** Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch for the generated views.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows each car''s **Generated set** (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and "from check-in photos" when those were used). **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car** make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.
- **Showroom background plates** (**Program settings**, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; **Make a new one** has Gemini make it again.

## The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)

Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.

- The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model''s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. **Program settings** > **Listings**: the scene for every car. On a car, **Studio photos** > **Scene** picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).
- No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car''s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.
- One set everywhere: once a car''s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car''s record.
- The check: Gemini checks each view against the car''s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.
- On a car, **Studio photos** shows each view beside the car''s own photos of that angle, marked **AI**. **Make again** makes one view again; **Take off the site** and **Put on the site**.
- **Listings** > **Photo standard** shows the fleet''s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini''s daily limit.
- Marketing set: **Make the marketing set** uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked **AI**; tick **In the ZIP** for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.
- Background plates (**Program settings**, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.

## Studio renders first (release 48)

- Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.
- On the site the renders come first, in this order: side profile (the nose to the left, the cover), front three-quarter, front, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. The car''s own photos follow, on the same branded background. They are never hidden.
- A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.
- The car page says **Rendered photos** above the gallery, with **See its real photos**.
- New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model''s daily limit.
- When a car''s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert ("Your car has new studio photos"), and Fleet gets "Studio photos live" in the next digest. Look the photos over.
- The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in **Data health**: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. <b class="gd-ui">This car</b> sets the car&#39;s own; the owner&#39;s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car&#39;s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>. Owners set the same limits in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot;, brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, tick <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b> and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu; customer service, Sales and Finance open it from <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Car map</b>) and field staff under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>, read only: every staff member sees where the cars are, and only Admins and fleet staff mark alerts as seen. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. A car&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s page show <b class="gd-ui">Where the car is</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">No tracker yet</b>). Each owner sees the location and trips of their own cars in the owner portal, never the renter or the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracker-events-evidence-and-pound-flags-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracker events, evidence and pound flags (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the map on the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab of <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>. It is off until the trackers are installed: an Admin turns on <b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Tracker event settings</b>.</p><p class="gd-p">On, each event makes one alert per car, kind and 30 minutes (never a flood), an evidence record, and a notice to the renter and to the car&#39;s owner:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Speeding over 180, 220 or 300 km/h</b>: one record per event, at the highest limit reached, with that limit&#39;s speeding charge of Settings &gt; Program ($500, $1,000 and $2,500 plus HST by default). One event is one charge: 226 km/h is $1,000, not $500 plus $1,000. The renter is told what the Tracker recorded, the charge and the clause (rental agreement 10.5).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Over the speeding alert level</b> (140 km/h) and <b class="gd-ui">harsh driving</b>: a friendly heads-up to the renter, no charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Left Ontario</b>, <b class="gd-ui">driving after the return time</b>, a tracker unplugged or tampered with: a notice with the clause. No set charge.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Left Canada</b>: urgent, once per crossing. Admins and on-duty Fleet get an alert, an email and a text at once (always on), Fleet gets an urgent To do, and the renter is told that leaving Canada needs written approval (rental agreement 10.1). Leaving Ontario for another province or a state reaches the same people the same way.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Driving at night</b> (off unless you turn it on): staff and the owner only. The agreement sets no curfew.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">At a pound</b>: see Pound flags below.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Tracker events</b> table shows each record: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, where it came from, how many readings it keeps, its seal (a SHA-256), the charge and the clause, and who was told.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To bill a speeding record, press <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> on its row (an Admin or Finance). The charge is added to the booking with the evidence record attached, and it is taken from the deposit first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The record goes into the dispute pack by itself, with the notice the renter got.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound flags</b>: a car whose tracker parks inside a pound lot&#39;s radius for 20 minutes is flagged. Fleet gets an urgent To do and alert, Fleet and Admins an email, and the renter is told to call.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Call the lot (its phone and hours are on the flag), then the renter. Keep the receipts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record the path</b>: the non-return charge ($1,000) or the theft recovery charge ($1,500) with the tow, impound and storage costs, <b class="gd-ui">Recovered, nothing to charge</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Not a pound</b>. Write what happened.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A charge still waits for its other evidence (the final late notice, the receipt) like every fee.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Pound lots</b>: the known Ontario lots, with name, address, phone and hours. It starts with the lots the Toronto and Peel police publish.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Find the pins from the addresses</b> once; a lot with no pin cannot flag a car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> a lot to add its hours, fix its details or type its pin, and tick <b class="gd-ui">I checked these details with the lot</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lot</b> for any other pound you know of.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Note</span><div>The renter&#39;s notice about a charge is always sent. The renter can mute the heads-up, and the owner can mute their alerts, in their own notification settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day&#39;s free AI share: a plate it finds is blurred so no character can be read (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or <b class="gd-ui">Not a plate: no plate visible</b> on a cover put where there is no plate.</p><p class="gd-p">To cover a plate yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> on the photo. The editor opens right under it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the box over the plate, or press <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The plate is blurred so no character can be read, only over the plate itself, with rounded corners and a soft edge. Nothing is drawn on a plate. A car with no front plate gets no box there. The studio photos Gemini makes have no plate at all: it is taken off cleanly, and a bumper without a plate is left as it is.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: Gemini makes each photo from the original, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The listing photos use no Cloudflare image processing: Gemini makes every photo and the site makes the sizes.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room&#39;s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings &gt; Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car&#39;s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-failed-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Failed photos</h2><p class="gd-p">The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> in its note; <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-primary-photo-is-always-the-front-exterior-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> is a flag and a filter in <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini, and generates its missing angles. A photo Gemini cannot make well stays off the site, flagged. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.</li><li>The same press checks the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Other detail</b> photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.</li><li>Every outside photo has the same room behind it: Gemini replaces the whole background from the original photo.</li><li>Every plate is blurred; nothing is drawn on it and there is no text anywhere else. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo every car with Gemini</b> (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) is the same as <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> on the Photo standard card.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-photo-standard-every-photo-made-by-gemini-release-45" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo standard: every photo made by Gemini (release 45)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every listing photo is made by Gemini from the original photo, never from a cut-out. Outside photos get their whole background replaced by the CarmaCars showroom, with nothing of the place they were taken in left. Inside photos are cleaned up (no clutter) and sharp from front to back. Every plate is blurred so no character can be read; no plate is drawn and there is no text anywhere else on the photo.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">The check.</b> A second Gemini look compares each new photo with the original and refuses it when the old background shows, the car is warped, another colour or model, has parts added or missing, a plate can be read, or there is text anywhere. The site also checks the edges are the dark showroom. A refused photo is made again, twice; then it stays off the site and is counted as flagged.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Missing angles.</b> Every car shows the standard set: front three-quarter, front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. An angle the car has no photo of is generated by Gemini from the car&#39;s own photos, in the same showroom, and marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b> on the listing (staff only). A real photo of that angle replaces it by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The order.</b> The front three-quarter is always first, then the other outside photos, then the inside ones. A car whose first photo would be an inside one shows no photos and cannot be published until it has an outside one; its front three-quarter is generated first.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">By itself.</b> Every 5 minutes the job brings the next cars to the standard, newest listed cars first, until every car is done (about a day for the whole fleet). A photo already at the standard is never made again unless you ask. <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the daily Gemini limit (2000 calls), the calls kept for new uploads (50) and the switch.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> (Admin and Fleet) shows each car: photos at the standard out of all, AI angles, flagged photos and the last run. <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> makes all of its photos again at once; <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> makes every photo of every car again. <b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on a car page does the same as Redo this car now.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-first-photo-plain-with-a-model-or-a-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b>, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>: the cover photo as it is (the default).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">With a model</b>: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b>: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Make it again</b> makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> (First photo &quot;flyer&quot; and First photo &quot;with a model&quot;); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-marketing-photos-in-other-scenes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Marketing photos in other scenes</h2><p class="gd-p">For Marketplace and social posts, a car&#39;s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b>, choose a scene, or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download (ZIP)</b> takes the set; the Marketplace kit&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the same set.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders&#39; own cars. To use another, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the reference photo</b> and pick one (the shareholders&#39; cars&#39; photos come first), or upload one. The scenes&#39; names and words are in the <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> setting.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-test-bookings-and-deleting-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Test bookings and deleting a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking made only to try the site, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a test booking</b> (Admins only; the reason is optional). <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking again</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b> adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. <b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b>, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b>. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day&#39;s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-every-view-generated-from-the-car-s-photos-release-47" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Every view generated from the car&#39;s photos (release 47)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car shows nine generated views: front three-quarter (always first), front, side profile, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats and trunk. Gemini makes each one from references, so the car is the real car and the room looks like a real showroom.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">What Gemini is sent.</b> The car&#39;s own photos (its exact colour, trim and wheels); when it has fewer than three, or none of that side, its newest check-in and check-out photos as well (only as references: they are never shown on the site). Then the sample view of that angle (for the camera position only), the stock photo of the model, and for an outside view the showroom background plate. The words describe each angle: camera height, lens, crop, the car centred, 45 degrees for a three-quarter. Plates blurred, no text, no logos added.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The check.</b> A second Gemini look compares the result with the real photos (same car, colour, wheels and trim, nothing warped, not a render) and with the angle. A refused view is made again, twice, told what was wrong; still refused, it is flagged and the car&#39;s real photo of that angle stays on the site.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">The real photos.</b> They stay in the car&#39;s record and on the Admin car page, marked as they were; the site shows the generated view of an angle in place of the real one only once it has passed. Generated views are marked <b class="gd-ui">AI generated</b> for staff only.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">By itself.</b> Every 5 minutes the job takes the front three-quarter of every car first (newest listed first), then the other angles, within the daily Gemini limit (about a day for the whole fleet). <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch for the generated views.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows each car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Generated set</b> (views made out of nine, being made, flagged, and &quot;from check-in photos&quot; when those were used). <b class="gd-ui">Redo this car now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Redo every car</b> make the generated views again too; the views on the site stay until the new ones pass.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Showroom background plates</b> (<b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, Admin): the room for front, side and rear views. Gemini made them once and a second look confirmed each looks like a real photo. Upload a real photo of a showroom (empty floor in the middle, no people, cars, signs or logos) to replace one or all three; <b class="gd-ui">Make a new one</b> has Gemini make it again.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-studio-set-every-car-photographed-the-same-way-release-4" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The studio set: every car photographed the same way (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car gets the same nine views, as if all were photographed in one studio on one day: the same angle, camera height, lens and framing for each view, the car facing the same way as the sample covers (the front three-quarter and the side with the nose to the left), plates taken off cleanly, the car itself unchanged.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The scene: every car stands in the same scene so the covers line up as you scroll: the dark dealership with the CarmaCars sign on the wall by default, with the model&#39;s name on the wall behind the car on the first photo. <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the scene for every car. On a car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Scene</b> picks another for that car only (highway, brick building and the other marketing scenes).</li><li>No photo of an angle? Gemini makes it from the car&#39;s other photos. A car with no photo at all gets its outside views from the stock photo of its model, in its own colour.</li><li>One set everywhere: once a car&#39;s front three-quarter is made, the site shows only its made views, in the standard order, the front three-quarter first: the same photo on the home page, the search cards, the car page, the partner feeds and in the sitemap. The real photos stay in the car&#39;s record.</li><li>The check: Gemini checks each view against the car&#39;s own photos: the same car (model, colour, wheels), the right angle, the nose the right way, the old background gone (the site also measures it), no readable plate. Smaller doubts (framing, a part the photos do not show) stop only the first two tries.</li><li>On a car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b> shows each view beside the car&#39;s own photos of that angle, marked <b class="gd-ui">AI</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> makes one view again; <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Put on the site</b>.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b> shows the fleet&#39;s progress: views made out of all, cars with their studio cover, and about how many days are left at Gemini&#39;s daily limit.</li><li>Marketing set: <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b> uses the studio views (the same angle and cover as the site) in the scene you choose, plus up to three lifestyle shots: an adult model with the car, styled like a luxury car advert, always fully dressed and tasteful. Each is marked <b class="gd-ui">AI</b>; tick <b class="gd-ui">In the ZIP</b> for the photos you want in a post. A lifestyle shot Gemini declines is skipped.</li><li>Background plates (<b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, Admin): one set per scene. Choose the scene, then upload a real photo of the place to replace one or all three.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-studio-renders-first-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Studio renders first (release 48)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every car gets the full studio set made from its own photos: same colour, wheels and trim, the same framing for every car.</li><li>On the site the renders come first, in this order: side profile (the nose to the left, the cover), front three-quarter, front, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk. The car&#39;s own photos follow, on the same branded background. They are never hidden.</li><li>A render goes live as soon as it passes the photo check. There is no approval step. To change one, open the car, <b class="gd-ui">Studio photos</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Make again</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take off the site</b>. Taking the side profile off makes the next render the cover.</li><li>The car page says <b class="gd-ui">Rendered photos</b> above the gallery, with <b class="gd-ui">See its real photos</b>.</li><li>New cars get their renders by themselves. To do every published car now: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Photo standard</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Render every published car</b>. The line beside it shows how many cars are done. It works within the image model&#39;s daily limit.</li><li>When a car&#39;s set is live, the owner gets an email and an alert (&quot;Your car has new studio photos&quot;), and Fleet gets &quot;Studio photos live&quot; in the next digest. Look the photos over.</li><li>The Cars filter lists one model per family (for example CLA-Class or 3 Series). The trim shows on the car. A car whose model family is not recognised is listed in <b class="gd-ui">Data health</b>: fix the typo, or ask for the family to be added.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'chapter', 'advertising-and-owner-recruitment', 'The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site''s own checks and published by themselves (the website''s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.

## The copy of a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.

1. The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car''s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.
2. Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what''s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.
3. To change a field press **Change**, then **Save and lock**. A locked field is kept by every new version. **Unlock** lets it be written again.
4. **Write again** asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car''s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.

> Good to know: The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car''s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.

## Landing pages and guides

**Settings**, then Search.

1. Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).
2. Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.
3. Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. Every page is in search: a page with no matching car lists the nearest similar ones instead.
4. Open **Edit** on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. **Write again** asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.

## Vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...

1. Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.
2. One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: **Index the place pages**, **Index the colour pages**, **Index the search term pages**, **Index the /buy pages**, **Index the detailing pages**, **Index the body shop pages**. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.
3. The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.
4. **Oldest model year with vehicle pages** (2005): cars from that year on. An older model year has no page in any tree (it answers not found) and is in no sitemap or list of years; a model with only older years has no page either.
5. **Financing disclaimer**: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.
6. Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (Pro, 6,144 MB, by default; Free, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.
7. Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.
8. Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People > Renters, the Leads tab.
9. Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.
10. Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. **Add trims for another model** adds a model that has none.
11. Catalog import: the last import and its counts. **Import now** asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.

> Good to know: A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car''s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.

## Stock photos on the vehicle pages

**Settings** > **Vehicle pages**, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: "Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons". The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.

1. Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet''s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked "not the exact year"; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.
2. The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.
3. Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press **Hide**. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.
4. **Pick again** asks for the next best photo; **Replace** takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.
5. **Show stock photos** in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).

> Good to know: Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer''s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.

## A car for sale

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car. On the For sale card, tick **For sale**, enter the Asking price and press **Save**.

1. The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.
2. Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.
3. "Find me this car" on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: **Owner leads**, Buyer leads), with a To do line.

## Search engines and business listings

**Settings**, then Site settings.

1. Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.
2. Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.
3. Business listings: press **Copy** beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.

> Good to know: Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.

## Place pages

Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. **Settings**, then Search.

1. Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.
2. Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.
3. Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.
4. Regions and places: Ontario is on, every city, town and neighbourhood in it; every other province, state and territory is off (kept, not deleted): its place pages answer not found and are in no sitemap. Tick a region to put its pages back.
5. Terms and services: change a term''s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term, switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for "price on request".
6. One page per service: terms people search with the same meaning are one group (car hire, cars for hire and vehicle rental are car rental; auto body repair is collision repair; auto detailing is car detailing). A synonym''s pages, by place and by car, send the visitor to its group''s page, which lists them ("Also searched as: ..."); only the group''s pages are in the sitemaps. Different services keep their own pages: interior and exterior detailing, ceramic coating, window tint, PPF, financing, leasing, lease takeover, insurance replacement rental and each mechanical service.

> Good to know: A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.

## Alternative searches

People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting ("Turo Alternative in Mississauga"), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.

## Requests from the place pages

The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in **To do**: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages offer to rent the model first and help find the car; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.

Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as "Auto services we arrange": a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. The pages say a trusted shop does the work, which CarmaCars arranges: each takes a request (a "Mechanical work to arrange" task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.

## One name, address and phone

The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.

## What search engines may read

**Settings**, **Vehicle pages**, **Search scope** says what search engines are invited to read:

- **Full (every page)**, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website''s CPU time as crawlers read them.
- **Core (about 23,000 pages)**: the fixed pages, the fleet''s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.

The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month''s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all ("try again tomorrow") until the month resets. People always get every page.

## IndexNow

**Search**, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.

### Index coverage

**Index coverage (Search Console sample)** shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.

### Longer pages from real data

Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR''s tolls, the city''s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car''s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.

> Good to know: After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on "Crawled - currently not indexed" (Indexing > Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.

### Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive

- **Positive pages**: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and **Request this exact car**; the checks refuse copy that says "not available", "we don''t have" or "we don''t offer".
- **Popular cars**: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says **Popular** with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.
- **Car figures**: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer''s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer''s colours, prices and equipment.
- **Parking**: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).
- **Events**: **Marketing** > **Event pages** lists the Toronto and GTA events with a "Rent a car for" page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.
- Pages for Turo searches: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.
- **GPS tracker**: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).
- **Airports**: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.
- **Renting vs owning**: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.
- **Languages**: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).
- **Reviews**: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. **Reviews** > **Add a customer review** enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer''s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.
- Sitemaps: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page''s languages), each with its own dates.

> Good to know: The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.

## Search footprint and the clicks goal (releases 35 and 36)

- The search pages are in 18 languages spoken across the GTA, with page families for places, landing needs, cars and models, events, airports, comparisons with other rental companies and renting vs owning.
- Real reviews show on every car and search page, each with where it was received. Staff add a review that came by text, call, email or another platform exactly as received, with a screenshot.
- The SEO page in the Admin portal follows Search Console: clicks and impressions by week, pages indexed, and the progress to the goal of 5 million clicks, with the page families that bring the most.

## The tracker pages, every service on every page, and the new page design (release 48)

**The GPS tracker and kill switch** has its own pages now:

- `/trackers`: the product page, with the price by number of cars, what it does, a comparison table, questions and the form. `/gps-tracker` sends people there.
- `/trackers/kill-switch-for-car`, `starter-interrupt-device`, `gps-tracker-for-rental-car`, `anti-theft-tracker-toronto`, `fleet-tracking`, `turo-host-gps-tracker` and `toll-and-ticket-billing`: one page for each way people search.
- `/trackers/install` and `/trackers/install/` followed by the place: "tracker install near me", one page per Ontario place, with the same gate as the place pages.

Every price on those pages comes from **Settings** > **Program settings** (the tracker tiers and the install price). While "Trackers can be installed" is off, every page says **Join the waitlist** with the words of "GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist" ("Shipping soon") and never says a tracker is in stock. Turn "Trackers can be installed" on when trackers can be installed: the same pages then take orders.

1. Someone joins the waitlist or pre-orders: a lead appears in **People** > **Renters** > **All leads** with the source "GPS tracker waitlist" or "GPS tracker pre-order", the number of cars and the price quoted, with its To do and the usual new-lead alert.
2. The person gets the email "You are on the waitlist" with their price. Nothing is charged.

**Every service on every page.** Each search page (landing pages, place pages, vehicle pages, the car page, events, airports) ends with the module **More from CarmaCars**: the tracker, List your car, chauffeur, delivery, coverage, monthly rentals, insurance replacement, rideshare, young drivers and the add-ons, each with its price when the database has one. `/services` lists every service with its pages.

**New landing pages**, edited like the others in **Settings** > **Search**: `rideshare`, `g2-licence`, `with-a-charger`, `with-flowers` and `with-child-seat`. The add-on pages show the add-on''s own price card from **Add-ons**, so change the price there, never in the copy.

**The page design.** Long pages are built from blocks: the short answer, the cars, price cards, the copy and the detail as folds (tap a heading to open it), questions, and on a phone a bar at the bottom with one button. The text is all still in the page for search engines.

> Good to know: a visitor who follows a Google, Bing, ChatGPT or Perplexity result to a place or vehicle page now gets the page at once. Before, a first visit could show "One moment, loading the page" for a second.
