',
  '<p class="gd-p">The text of every car page, the landing pages for each area and way of renting, and the guides are written every day by a scheduled Claude session from the facts in the database, checked with the site&#39;s own checks and published by themselves (the website&#39;s Workers AI writer is off, so the free AI allowance stays with the staff assistant). Nobody has to type or review anything. You can still change any line; what you change is kept.</p><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-the-copy-of-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The copy of a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car, then its Listing tab. The same card is on the listing review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The card says who wrote the text: a plain copy from the car&#39;s facts while the written copy is prepared (the next daily batch), then the batch (claude-batch) or Workers AI.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every field is shown: search title and description, heading, introduction, highlights, good for, what&#39;s included, pickup and delivery, requirements, questions and the photo descriptions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To change a field press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save and lock</b>. A locked field is kept by every new version. <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> lets it be written again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version now. A new version is also written by itself when the car&#39;s facts change: its rates, specs, area or photos.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The checks refuse long dashes, sales words, the numbered company, any number that is not in the car&#39;s facts (a price, a seat count) and equipment the facts do not list. A version that fails is asked again with the problems named; if it still fails, the page keeps its current text and it is tried again later.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-landing-pages-and-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Landing pages and guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Today: the Workers AI used for search copy and in all, and IndexNow (addresses waiting and sent).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Car copy: every real car, who wrote its text, and whether its facts changed since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Landing pages: each place and way of renting, whether it is in search, its cars and who wrote it. Every page is in search: a page with no matching car lists the nearest similar ones instead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a page or a guide to change its text. Edited fields are locked. <b class="gd-ui">Write again</b> asks for a new version; on a guide, the brief says what it must cover.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>. A page for every make, model, model year and Canadian trim of every year, at carmacars.ca/cars/make/model/year/trim, with our cars below it; each trim also in every place and in 12 colours (a black 2020 Volkswagen Jetta Sportline in Mississauga, for example); every page again for sale (carmacars.ca/buy/...) and for each search term: renting (car hire), sale (financing), detailing (ceramic coating) and body shop (bumper repair), at carmacars.ca/t/term/...</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pages: how many pages each level and each tier has, the total, and how many are in search. Every page is in search by default; nothing needs setting up.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One switch per tier takes it out of search at once: <b class="gd-ui">Index the place pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the colour pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the search term pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the /buy pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the detailing pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Index the body shop pages</b>. Off, those pages stay visible but leave the sitemaps and search.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The places are the place list of the local search release (every city, town and neighbourhood, with GTA and country levels); until it is filled, the area landing pages. The search terms are edited with them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Oldest model year with vehicle pages</b> (2005): cars from that year on. An older model year has no page in any tree (it answers not found) and is in no sitemap or list of years; a model with only older years has no page either.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Financing disclaimer</b>: the text on financing and leasing pages. CarmaCars never says it lends or leases.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Database: its size against the cap the catalog and places imports keep under: the cap of the Database plan (Pro, 6,144 MB, by default; Free, 450 MB). IndexNow: the addresses sent today, where the sweep is, and any back-off; nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Each page is built from data: the EPA fuel-use ratings in litres per 100 km, the cost to drive 100 km at the gas or electricity price set here, what changed from the year before, how a trim differs from the others, similar models, and the rental questions from the program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Below the facts: our cars of that exact year, model and trim, then the same model in other years, then similar cars free now, and Request it, which sends an enquiry to People &gt; Renters, the Leads tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Settings: every page is in search; the switch per tier above is the only way to take a tier out.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Canadian trims: open a model and type one line per run of years, entry trim first: 2020-2021: Comfortline, Highline, Sportline, Execline. Your lines are kept by every import; empty them to go back to the CarmaCars list. <b class="gd-ui">Add trims for another model</b> adds a model that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Catalog import: the last import and its counts. <b class="gd-ui">Import now</b> asks for a new one; it runs at the next daily check, at 07:17 UTC.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A car joins its pages by itself once it is on the site: its make, model, year and trim are read from the car. A trim that names several (S / SE / R-Line) leaves the car on the year page only; set the car&#39;s trim to one Canadian name to put it on the trim page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-stock-photos-on-the-vehicle-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stock photos on the vehicle pages</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, card Stock photos. The vehicle pages show a real photo of the make, model and generation at the top (a 2015 Camry page shows a Camry of the 2012 to 2017 generation), with the credit always under it: &quot;Photo: author, licence, Wikimedia Commons&quot;. The place pages and the detailing and body shop pages show a photo of a road, a car being detailed or a body shop. Our own cars always show their own photos.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing to set up: the photos come by themselves every day, our fleet&#39;s models and the popular models first. Only free licences are used (public domain, CC0, CC BY, CC BY-SA), from Wikimedia Commons, or Openverse when Commons has none. A year without a photo of its own generation shows the nearest photo of the model, marked &quot;not the exact year&quot;; a model with no photo keeps the studio drawing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The card shows how many models and model years have a photo, the popular models still without one, and the last run.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a make to see its photos. A wrong car, a poor photo or a photo you do not want: press <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b>. The page goes back to the studio drawing at once, and that photo is never picked again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pick again</b> asks for the next best photo; <b class="gd-ui">Replace</b> takes a photo you found on Wikimedia Commons: paste its address (https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:...). Either is done at the next daily run, after its licence is checked. A photo whose licence is not allowed is refused, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show stock photos</b> in the settings above turns every stock photo off at once (on by default).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Never upload or use a photo from Google, a dealer or a manufacturer&#39;s site here: only Wikimedia Commons files, with the credit the page shows.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-a-car-for-sale" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car for sale</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car. On the For sale card, tick <b class="gd-ui">For sale</b>, enter the Asking price and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The car then shows at the top of its /buy pages (its make, model, year and trim) with the asking price, the only time a page says a car is for sale.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Untick it when the car is sold or no longer for sale: the pages say so at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Find me this car&quot; on the /buy pages sends a buyer lead to Sales (staff portal: <b class="gd-ui">Owner leads</b>, Buyer leads), with a To do line.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-engines-and-business-listings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search engines and business listings</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Search engines: paste the Google Search Console value (HTML tag) or the file name (HTML file), and the Bing value. The steps are on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Business name, address and phone: the exact text for every listing, and the description and categories.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Business listings: press <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> beside each line and paste it into Google Business Profile, Bing Places, Apple Business Connect, Yelp, Yellow Pages and Facebook. Tick each one when it is done.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changed pages are sent to IndexNow (Bing and the other engines that use it) by themselves. Google reads the sitemap: submit carmacars.ca/sitemap.xml once in Search Console.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">Every place we have, from a country down to a neighbourhood, gets a page for every term people search with: renting (car hire, SUV rental, monthly car rental ...), buying help (used cars, car financing ...), detailing (ceramic coating, window tint ...) and body work (collision repair, dent repair ...). Each page is written from real data only: the distance from us, the delivery price within our reach, the nearest airport, the landmarks near it, our live cars and the places around it. A place far from Toronto says we serve the Toronto area and takes a request instead. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Search.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Place pages: four switches, one for each family, put the pages in search and in the sitemaps. All four are on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every place page is in search and filled with its own data; there is no quality gate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Delivery reach: places within this distance of our location are offered delivery. Database size cap: the places import stops before the database passes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Regions and places: Ontario is on, every city, town and neighbourhood in it; every other province, state and territory is off (kept, not deleted): its place pages answer not found and are in no sitemap. Tick a region to put its pages back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Terms and services: change a term&#39;s title or what is true about it, point a synonym to another term, switch a term off, or add one. Give a service a starting price, or leave it empty for &quot;price on request&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">One page per service: terms people search with the same meaning are one group (car hire, cars for hire and vehicle rental are car rental; auto body repair is collision repair; auto detailing is car detailing). A synonym&#39;s pages, by place and by car, send the visitor to its group&#39;s page, which lists them (&quot;Also searched as: ...&quot;); only the group&#39;s pages are in the sitemaps. Different services keep their own pages: interior and exterior detailing, ceramic coating, window tint, PPF, financing, leasing, lease takeover, insurance replacement rental and each mechanical service.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A region has pages once the places workflow has loaded it: GitHub, Actions, places, Run workflow, with the regions or all. The run loads Ontario first and names any region it skipped because of the size cap.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-alternative-searches" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Alternative searches</h2><p class="gd-p">People also search for an alternative to another service. Turo alternative, RideAlike alternative and Luup alternative for rideshare drivers have their place pages like every way of renting (&quot;Turo Alternative in Mississauga&quot;), in the sitemaps. Each page says plainly that CarmaCars is not affiliated with the company named and says nothing about that company. Nothing to set up.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-requests-from-the-place-pages" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Requests from the place pages</h2><p class="gd-p">The buying help, detailing and body shop pages, and the pages of places beyond our reach, have a request form. Each request is a lead with a task in <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>: detailing and body shop requests are due within an hour of opening and show in Today. Buying help pages offer to rent the model first and help find the car; the notice at the top is set under Place pages.</p><p class="gd-p">Mechanical work has pages too, under the body shop pages and listed apart as &quot;Auto services we arrange&quot;: a mechanic, oil changes, brakes, tires and winter tires, towing, batteries and boosts, alignment, transmission and engine repair, diagnostics, inspections and the Ontario safety certificate, emissions, AC, exhaust and suspension. The pages say a trusted shop does the work, which CarmaCars arranges: each takes a request (a &quot;Mechanical work to arrange&quot; task, due within an hour of opening) and offers a rental while the car is in. They have no questions of their own; their per car pages (for each make, model, year and trim) say the same and take the same request.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-one-name-address-and-phone" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One name, address and phone</h2><p class="gd-p">The footer, the contact page, the structured data and every business listing show the business address of Site settings. Keep it the address renters come to, and change it there only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-what-search-engines-may-read" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What search engines may read</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle pages</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Search scope</b> says what search engines are invited to read:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Full (every page)</b>, the default: every vehicle, place, colour, search term and for-sale page is in the sitemaps and open to crawlers. It costs more of the website&#39;s CPU time as crawlers read them.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Core (about 23,000 pages)</b>: the fixed pages, the fleet&#39;s cars, the landing pages, the guides and the vehicle pages down to the trim. The other pages stay up for people, but robots.txt keeps crawlers out and they are in no sitemap.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">The change takes effect within minutes, with no deploy. In either scope, from 70% of the month&#39;s included CPU time crawlers get no catalog page at all (&quot;try again tomorrow&quot;) until the month resets. People always get every page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-indexnow" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">IndexNow</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Search</b>, Today shows IndexNow in two lines. Changed pages: a car, a landing page or a guide that changed, sent first and on their own, 100 at a time; a refusal waits an hour, then longer, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours. Sweep: the priority list once a week, 1,000 addresses a request (Program settings); a refusal from Bing waits until the next day, a day longer for each refusal in a row, and a server error 10 minutes, doubling up to 6 hours, then the sweep goes on from where it was.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Index coverage</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Index coverage (Search Console sample)</b> shows, by day, how many of the addresses the gsc workflow inspected Google knows, how many of those are indexed (the share Search Console itself counts), the priority pages indexed, the crawled and discovered but not indexed, and apart the addresses still unknown to Google (most of the long tail). A car page is sent to IndexNow again whenever its copy, prices or photos change, and each place page now names its drive time, the landmarks and places near it and the real cars with their prices.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Longer pages from real data</h3><p class="gd-p">Every place page, landing page, car page and vehicle page has sections written from its own data: the cars and their daily, weekly and 30-day prices and deposits (or the nearest similar cars when none match), the delivery fee, the distance and drive time from us, the nearest airport and GO station, the highways and the 407 ETR&#39;s tolls, the city&#39;s parking rule, the age, licence, coverage and deposit rules, the fee schedule, the car&#39;s figures and the cost to drive 100 km, and questions answered from those facts. Nothing to set up: the stops, hotels and specs come from the seo-data workflow every week, each with its source shown on the page.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>After a release that changes these pages, press Validate fix in Search Console on &quot;Crawled - currently not indexed&quot; (Indexing &gt; Pages). Google has no way to press it for you.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Release 36: more pages, more data, every page positive</h3><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Positive pages</b>: a search page never says what we lack. A page whose own list is empty shows the cars ready to book now and <b class="gd-ui">Request this exact car</b>; the checks refuse copy that says &quot;not available&quot;, &quot;we don&#39;t have&quot; or &quot;we don&#39;t offer&quot;.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Popular cars</b>: a car with more than its share of the requests (Program settings, Demand steering: 25% by default) is placed lower in Trending (no higher than 6th), its page says <b class="gd-ui">Popular</b> with similar cars first, and the search pages list it after the others. A pin still leads.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Car figures</b>: every car and vehicle page shows what the free sources give, each with its source: the manufacturer&#39;s price, production years and plants (Wikidata), dimensions (NHTSA vPIC, Canada), recall campaigns (NHTSA and Transport Canada), the parts owners complain about most (NHTSA), charging, equipment, and ratings out of 10 with how each is worked out (fuel economy, performance, space, crash safety, recall record, parkability). The seo-data workflow loads them weekly; a curated CSV adds the manufacturer&#39;s colours, prices and equipment.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Parking</b>: place, event and airport pages list the parking lots, garages and streets with parking nearby (OpenStreetMap).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Events</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Marketing</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Event pages</b> lists the Toronto and GTA events with a &quot;Rent a car for&quot; page. Add an event, or set its dates once the organiser announces them; until then the page says the months it is usually held. Sales sees the same list on its Marketing page.</li><li>Pages for Turo searches: five landing pages for people searching Turo cancellations, deposits, fees, damage and missed handovers. They describe our own process and say CarmaCars is not affiliated with Turo.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">GPS tracker</b>: its page (/gps-tracker) and a short section on the search pages, from Program settings (name, prices, features, details; off hides both).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports</b>: a page for Pearson and Billy Bishop: the car delivered to the terminal at the standard delivery price.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Renting vs owning</b>: a page per popular model year (and the nearest cities) with the monthly cost of owning, line by line with sources, against our monthly rate. The financing rate and term, kilometres, depreciation and cleaning are Program settings; insurance and parking figures are added with their source.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Languages</b>: the landing, event and airport pages in 18 languages (French, Punjabi, Mandarin, Cantonese, Arabic, Urdu, Tagalog, Spanish, Portuguese, Italian, Tamil, Farsi, Korean, Russian, Hindi, Gujarati, Vietnamese, Polish) at carmacars.ca/fr/... The seo-i18n workflow translates the templates once; a language is in search and named to Google only once 90% of its text is translated (Program settings).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: real reviews show on every car page and search page with their source. <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Add a customer review</b> enters one that came another way (Turo, an earlier platform, a text, a call, email, in person, Google): the first name and last initial, the source, the date, the rating, the customer&#39;s words exactly as received, and a screenshot if you have one. Never write or change a review for a customer. Hide one only for cause.</li><li>Sitemaps: two more files, the new page families and the language versions (with each page&#39;s languages), each with its own dates.</li></ul><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The Cantonese pages are translated by a person (the translation model has no Cantonese): until then they stay out of search.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-search-footprint-and-the-clicks-goal-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search footprint and the clicks goal (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The search pages are in 18 languages spoken across the GTA, with page families for places, landing needs, cars and models, events, airports, comparisons with other rental companies and renting vs owning.</li><li>Real reviews show on every car and search page, each with where it was received. Staff add a review that came by text, call, email or another platform exactly as received, with a screenshot.</li><li>The SEO page in the Admin portal follows Search Console: clicks and impressions by week, pages indexed, and the progress to the goal of 5 million clicks, with the page families that bring the most.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides-the-tracker-pages-every-service-on-every-page-and-the-new-pa" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The tracker pages, every service on every page, and the new page design (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The GPS tracker and kill switch</b> has its own pages now:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers</span>: the product page, with the price (free for vehicle owners and for the first pre-orders, then the pre-order price, then the regular price after launch), the install and the monthly service by number of cars, what it does, a comparison table, questions and the form. <span class="gd-url">/gps-tracker</span> sends people there.</li><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers/kill-switch-for-car</span>, <span class="gd-url">starter-interrupt-device</span>, <span class="gd-url">gps-tracker-for-rental-car</span>, <span class="gd-url">anti-theft-tracker-toronto</span>, <span class="gd-url">fleet-tracking</span>, <span class="gd-url">turo-host-gps-tracker</span> and <span class="gd-url">toll-and-ticket-billing</span>: one page for each way people search.</li><li><span class="gd-url">/trackers/install</span> and <span class="gd-url">/trackers/install/</span> followed by the place: &quot;tracker install near me&quot;, one page per Ontario place, with the same gate as the place pages.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Every price on those pages comes from <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tracker&#39;s prices and the install price). While &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is off, every page says <b class="gd-ui">Join the waitlist</b> with the words of &quot;GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist&quot; (&quot;Shipping soon&quot;) and never says a tracker is in stock. Turn &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; on when trackers can be installed: the same pages then take orders.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Someone joins the waitlist or pre-orders: a lead appears in <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All leads</b> with the source &quot;GPS tracker waitlist&quot; or &quot;GPS tracker pre-order&quot;, the number of cars and the price quoted, with its To do and the usual new-lead alert. The source ends with &quot;(vehicle owner)&quot; for an owner and &quot;(free tracker)&quot; for a free pre-order. The form has a box &quot;My car is listed with CarmaCars (vehicle owner)&quot;: when the email is not an active owner&#39;s, the lead says &quot;check before the install&quot;, so confirm the person is an owner before the free tracker is promised.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The person gets a confirmation email that says how they joined (vehicle owner, pre-order or waitlist), what the tracker costs them, the install price and the monthly service for their number of cars. Nothing is charged.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Every service on every page.</b> Each search page (landing pages, place pages, vehicle pages, the car page, events, airports) ends with the module <b class="gd-ui">More from CarmaCars</b>: the tracker, List your car, chauffeur, delivery, coverage, monthly rentals, insurance replacement, rideshare, young drivers and the add-ons, each with its price when the database has one. <span class="gd-url">/services</span> lists every service with its pages.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">New landing pages</b>, edited like the others in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Search</b>: <span class="gd-url">rideshare</span>, <span class="gd-url">g2-licence</span>, <span class="gd-url">with-a-charger</span>, <span class="gd-url">with-flowers</span> and <span class="gd-url">with-child-seat</span>. The add-on pages show the add-on&#39;s own price card from <b class="gd-ui">Add-ons</b>, so change the price there, never in the copy.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">The page design.</b> Long pages are built from blocks: the short answer, the cars, price cards, the copy and the detail as folds (tap a heading to open it), questions, and on a phone a bar at the bottom with one button. The text is all still in the page for search engines.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>a visitor who follows a Google, Bing, ChatGPT or Perplexity result to a place or vehicle page now gets the page at once. Before, a first visit could show &quot;One moment, loading the page&quot; for a second.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'settings', 'chapter', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.

## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking''s all-in price a day) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
1. RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Shifts published by themselves (on): the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day from November 23, 2026), how many days ahead (14) and the first day they may be published for; a handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own. Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

![](/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program; pins: 1 25.8 22.0, 2 27.8 49.0")


## Lead-time pricing

A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open **Settings**, then **Program settings**: Lead-time pricing is at the top.

1. The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).
2. The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); **Add a tier** adds one, **Remove** takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.
3. **Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer** is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.
4. Press **Save lead-time pricing**. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.

| What it touches | How |
| --- | --- |
| The rental charge | The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, "Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%". Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons |
| When it is worked out | When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. "From $X a day" stays at the base rate |
| When it is locked | On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage |
| Other discounts | The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it |
| Owner revenue and commissions | Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts |
| Staff | Change it on a booking under **More options** on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted |

> Tip: A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: **Vehicles** > the car > **Rates** > Lead-time pricing for this car.
## Vehicle class rules

Open **Settings**, then **Vehicle class rules**. How a new car''s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.

1. The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.
2. Press **Add a rule** or **Change**: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.
3. **Try a car** gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.
4. **Delete** removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.

> Tip: A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.

## Official ServiceOntario forms

The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher''s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. Each form shows "Mapping to check" (a draft is ready) or "Official PDF in use". Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.
2. Choose **Preview with**: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press **Download a filled preview** and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.
3. Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or "Signed here by hand, in ink"), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. **Earlier mappings** lists every save, with who and when; **Load** puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners > Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.
4. Press **Checked: use for owners**. Every owner''s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with **Record an official form signed in ink**. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.
5. A new version from ServiceOntario? Press **Upload the official fillable PDF**: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.

> Good to know: SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company''s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner''s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form''s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.

## Blind Spot rental agreement

We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental''s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars'' rental agreement and Blind Spot''s own. Blind Spot''s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press **Upload Blind Spot''s PDF** and choose Blind Spot''s blank form (2 pages, A4).
2. Press **Download the filled sample**: a made-up booking on the form. **Sample billed to an insurer** also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.
3. On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars'' HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative''s signature instead of Sam''s.
4. Press **Checked: use for bookings**. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.
5. Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.
6. A new version of Blind Spot''s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for **Checked: use for bookings**, and bookings keep the version in use until then.

> Good to know: Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.

The renter''s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking''s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter''s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the "Your signed rental agreement" email. Admin > Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.

## Agreements to sign: investors and staff

Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person''s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).

1. Investor: open **People** > **Investors** and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press **Send the agreement to sign**. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press **Send to sign**.
2. Once the investor signs, the agreement shows **Awaiting countersignature** on the investor''s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press **Countersign**. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.
3. Staff: open **People** > **Team**. Under Staff agreements, press **Send the agreement to sign** beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.
4. A field staff member''s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.
5. They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.
6. Already sent or signed with old terms? Press **Send a new agreement** beside the person: it is filled with the current terms (for staff who live in Canada: Canada, CAD, Interac e-Transfer or direct deposit) and sent to sign the same way. The one waiting is withdrawn; a signed one stays on file, marked superseded, and keeps their portal open until they sign the new one. Someone in Canada still on the old terms (the Philippines, USD, OnlineJobs.ph) shows **Lives in Canada: needs the Canadian terms**, and a To do lists them.
7. Your own PDF instead? **Send a PDF to sign** still works.
8. Sent by mistake? Press **Withdraw** and give the reason.

## The user guides

**Settings** > **Guides**. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.

1. Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.
2. Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press **Show the preview** to see it as people will. Press **Save the draft**; each save is kept in the section''s history.
3. Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press **Add a chapter**. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.
4. Press **Publish version** (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.
5. The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.

## The guides keep up by themselves

After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.

1. Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.
2. The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal''s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.
3. Such a section says **Changed automatically on** and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide''s editor. Not right? Open the section and press **Revert**: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.
4. This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section''s history. There is nothing to review.
5. A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.

> Tip: The card "The guides keep up by themselves" at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.

## Insurers and the other lists

1. Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in **Money** > **Insurers**.
2. To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press **Add**.
3. Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.

## Promo codes: end dates and reminders

**Settings**, **Promo codes**.

- Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.
- A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.
- A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with "This code has expired".
- A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.
- The list shows each code''s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.

## Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage

**Settings** > **Card coverage** is the list renters see at `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage` and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.

1. The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer''s own document, and when it was last checked.
2. Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press **Save**. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.
3. A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer''s own document unticked and the summary''s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer''s guide.
4. Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.

> Tip: A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer''s guide.

## Reviews: review requests and Google

**Settings** > **Reviews**: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.

1. When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.
2. The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile''s own review link.
3. Google Business Profile: press **Connect Google** and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.
4. A clear match stops that renter''s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press **Confirm**, **Not this renter** or **Match to a booking**.

> Tip: Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and "I already left a review", Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.

### Pair the card reader
**Settings** > **Card reader**. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open **Settings**, then **Generate pairing code**. Type the three words in **Pairing code**, name the reader (Front desk) and press **Pair reader**. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. **Remove** takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account''s statement descriptor.

### Rewards
**Settings** > **Rewards**. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter''s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.

1. **Ways to earn**: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend''s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows "Received reward points"), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter''s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).
2. **Tiers**: Gold from 1,000 points earned in 12 months, Platinum from 15,000, Black from 60,000 (below Gold a renter is a Member). Points earned count, so using points never lowers a tier. Press **Change** on a tier for its name and points. Tiers give perks, not discounts; tier codes issued before release 40 work until they end.
3. **Perks**: Instant Book (Gold), Any car, any time (Platinum) and a free rental day a year (Black). Each tier keeps the perks below it. **Change** a perk to move it to another tier, reword it or switch it off. **Change the response time** sets how fast Fleet answers an Any car request (4 hours); the open ones are listed with their answer-by time.
4. Points and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code, except the Black tier''s free day: CarmaCars pays for it, and the owner''s payout is worked out on the price before it.
4. **Google reviews claimed** lists every claim; **Reverse** takes the points back with a reason. **A renter''s points**: find the renter, then **Add or take off points** with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).
5. **Emails and notices to renters**: every Rewards email, each also a notice in the renter''s portal (a text only when they have no email): the welcome, points earned, a new tier, the free day, close to the next tier, points waiting, the 7-day reminder, the free day ending, the monthly statement and the birthday and holiday rewards. Each shows how many went in the last 30 days. **Preview** shows the email with sample values; **Turn off** stops it; **Change** sets the timings or switches them all off. Marketing ones carry an unsubscribe link and never go to someone who unsubscribed.
6. **Birthday and holiday rewards**: a percent off the rental charge by tier for a pickup near the renter''s birthday (7 days either side) or on a holiday weekend: Platinum 10%, Black 20%; Gold is off (0%) until you give it a percent. The bigger one applies, never both, never below the car''s lowest daily price, never on insurer or Owner Bookings. The request or offer keeps it. **Change** a tier for its percents or to switch it off; the holidays are listed with their next weekend: **Turn off**, **Remove** or **Add a holiday** by its date rule.

### Setup checklist
**Settings** shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars'' own accounts. **Add to Apple Wallet** stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker''s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.


Program: **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device''s own phone and messages apps.

## Stuck? help

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Stuck? help**: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. **Where people get stuck**, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.

### API access (Claude and scripts)

Settings > **API access** connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring ("hire Ana as customer service"). **Connect from Claude**: in Claude, Settings > Connectors > Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press **Allow**. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, **Make a key**: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; **Revoke** stops it at once. The **Call log** lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.

### The logo

The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings > **Site settings**, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).

## Deposits stay as holds (release 28)

Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking''s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with **Re-authorize the hold**: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.

**Program settings**: **Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)** is on: Stripe approved it for the account. Every deposit hold (the pay link, the saved card, **Re-authorize the hold**, the reader) asks for a longer authorization, about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise; a card that cannot gets the standard hold by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in **Fees**, editable as every fee.

## Updated terms to accept

**Settings** > **Updated terms**. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with **Requires acceptance** on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.

1. Press **Publish a version**. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).
2. Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and **What changed**: people read this summary first.
3. Paste **The new text**. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site''s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site''s page.
4. Leave **Requires acceptance** on and press **Publish a version**.
5. Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees **We''ve updated our terms** full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.
6. **Accepted** on each version opens who accepted it and when.

> Good to know: It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.

> Good to know: Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.

### Card processing fee for a debit deposit
Program settings: **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)** and **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)** (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.

## My profile and name changes (release 34)
Settings > **My profile** has your display name, **Request a name change** for your legal name, your phone number and **Change my password**. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.

## AI auto-replies (release 36)

**Settings** > **Program settings**, the AI auto-replies group, answers common questions by itself, only from the FAQ (**Site content**), within Workers AI''s free daily allowance. Each channel has its switch, on by default: texts to the CarmaCars number, emails to the inboxes listed (help@in.carmacars.ca), the website live chat, WhatsApp, Facebook Page messages and Instagram messages.

1. A question the FAQ answers gets the answer at once. A text asked between 1 am and 5 am is answered at 5 am (the quiet hours are settings).
2. When the FAQ does not answer it, or the model is not sure enough (70%), nothing is sent: a text stays in Messages for staff, and an email or a Meta message becomes a To do for customer service, **Answer** and the question.
3. Each person gets at most 5 automatic answers a day, never while a staff member texted them in the last 2 hours, and none once the day''s free AI allowance is used.
4. The card **AI auto-replies: the last answers** shows today''s answers and the last questions, with what was sent or why not.

Messenger, Instagram and WhatsApp need the Meta app''s webhook set to https://carmacars.ca/api/webhooks/meta with the verify token shown in the settings, and the Worker secrets META_APP_SECRET (and WHATSAPP_TOKEN with the WhatsApp number id). TikTok has no inbound message path for businesses, so it is not answered.

## Address suggestions (release 36)

The address fields suggest Canadian addresses from the site''s own address database (Statistics Canada''s Open Database of Addresses, loaded by the addresses workflow, Ontario first). Google is asked only for what the database does not have, and only when its key is set.

## Card coverage: the facts the booking check uses (release 35)

Each card also has: **Network** (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), **Includes rental car damage coverage (CDW)** (Yes, No or Unknown), **Vehicle types not covered** (comma separated: exotic, luxury, truck, van, off_road, antique, motorcycle, limousine, rv), **Must decline the rental company''s CDW** and **Must pay the full rental on the card**. A renter on card coverage picks their card from this list; the site checks it against the car''s value (the Black Book value or the estimate on the car), the car''s type and the length of the rental, and refuses a card that does not cover it. Unknown sends the renter to staff review. Exotic makes are listed in **Program** > **Coverage checks**.

## Fuel prices and delivery (release 35)

- **Program** > **Fuel and charging at the return**: the local pump prices of regular, premium and diesel (a litre), the multiplier (1.25), the refuelling fee ($20), the price a kWh for electric cars ($0.40), and the tank and battery sizes for a car without its own. Update the pump prices every week: **Today** reminds you after 7 days.
- **Airports and delivery** > **Delivery rate and origin**: the base fee each way ($75), the km it includes from the company''s location (15), the rate per km after them ($2), and the straight line to road distance factor (1.3) used when the maps service gives no road distance. A car whose rate card has its own delivery or pickup fee keeps it; every other car follows the base.

## Automatic answers and email budgets (release 36)

- Automatic answers: each channel (text, email, chat, social messages) switches on or off, with the quiet hours, the daily limit per person and how sure the answer must be. The last answers and the questions left for a person show in settings and under renter messages; a question it cannot answer becomes a To do. They stay inside the free daily AI allowance.
- Email budgets: Settings, Usage shows the real daily email capacity of all our sending services together (Cloudflare included), and when a service is not sending, why. Receipts, signed copies and staff messages always go.
- First photo: each listing chooses its first photo, the plain car, a car-show photo with a model, or a flyer with the live price; the flyer is made again when the price changes.
- Rewards: points for a photo with a review and for every rental after the first; every way to earn is on the renter''s Rewards page.

## Owner emails: trips and the week (release 41)

Owners are not emailed when a booking comes in, is confirmed or changes, because many bookings are cancelled (owner_new_booking, owner_booking_confirmed and owner_booking_changed are off, with their texts and notices). They are emailed when a trip is complete and the car is back (owner_trip_completed: the car, dates, days, distance driven if recorded and their share, which says it shows on the next statement while the booking''s revenue is hidden from them), and every Monday at about 9:00 Toronto time (owner_weekly_summary: per car, last week''s trips with their share, the confirmed bookings of the next 14 days with dates only, and the month so far, provisional), only when there was activity. Only bookings that count toward the owner''s revenue are used, never Owner Bookings or Turo trips. The Monday email has a switch in Program settings: **Weekly summary email to owners** (on by default).

## Call helper (release 43)

**Settings**, **Call helper**: what staff read inside the caller pop-up while on a call. A change shows on the next call.

1. **Greetings**: one for each kind of caller (a caller we do not know, a renter with a booking, a renter with no booking now, a lead, a car owner, a staff member). Press **Change** and type what to say. `{staff}` becomes the first name of the person on the phone, `{caller}` the caller''s first name, `{booking}` the booking number and `{car}` the car. A greeting that is off, or that needs a name we do not have, falls back to the one for a caller we do not know, which stays on.
2. **Situations**: one button each. **Add a situation** or **Change**: the name on the button, then the steps, one a line (3 to 6 is best, 8 at most). Write a link to a page as `[Bookings](/bookings)`: an Admin gets the Admin page and staff get their own. Words in "quotes" are shown as what to say. **Order** sets the place of the button; switch **On** off to hide one, or **Remove** it.
3. **Quick answers**: the question, the answer, and more search words staff might type.
4. **Numbers from the settings**: never type an amount, a number of days or a percentage. Write its word in braces from this list, for example `{late_grace}` or `{deposit_tiers}`: staff read today''s value from Program settings, Fee defaults and Deposit tiers, and it changes the day the setting does. A word in braces that is not in the list is refused when you save.

Every change is in the audit log with the words before and after.

## Texts and email by message type (release 48)
Program settings, **Texts and email by message type**, lists each message that can go by text with how many texts it sent in the last 30 days. Turn on **Email ready for production** once Amazon SES is out of its sandbox: then only the urgent messages keep their texts (the pickup details and codes, a late return, a failed payment, a declined deposit), and every other message goes by email, by text only when the person has no email address or their email bounced. Press **Change** on a row to send that message by email only, text only, or text and email (the person''s choice). The deposit link, sign-in codes, staff alerts and texts typed by staff always stay texts. While the switch is off nothing changes.

## Deposits by e-Transfer or cash, and tips

1. **Deposit by e-Transfer or cash: a multiple of the deposit** (on) and its multiplier (2): a $300 deposit is $600 by e-Transfer or cash. A debit or prepaid card keeps its own multiplier. An amount set on one booking wins.
2. **Tips** (on): the pay page, the receipt and the after-trip email offer 10, 15 or 20% or an amount; **the salesperson''s share** (5000: half, the rest to the handover).

## The tracker''s price and duplicate leads (release 48)

In **Settings** > **Program settings**:

- "GPS tracker product: the monthly price per car by number of cars": the tracker''s monthly price per car by number of cars. It starts at $25 for 1 or 2 cars, $20 for 3 to 9 and $15 for 10 or more. "GPS tracker product: the install price": the install, $150 once per car. The tracker pages, the services module and the waitlist email all read these.
- "GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist": the words beside "Join the waitlist" while "Trackers can be installed" is off.
- "Duplicate leads: join a new website form to the person''s open lead" and "Duplicate leads: how many days back the rule looks": whether a new website form joins the person''s open lead by itself, and how many days back it looks.
', 'Settings', 'Site, program settings, official forms mapping, insurers and the other lists.',
  'Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.

## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking''s all-in price a day) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
1. RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Shifts published by themselves (on): the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day from November 23, 2026), how many days ahead (14) and the first day they may be published for; a handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own. Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

![](/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program; pins: 1 25.8 22.0, 2 27.8 49.0")


## Lead-time pricing

A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open **Settings**, then **Program settings**: Lead-time pricing is at the top.

1. The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).
2. The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); **Add a tier** adds one, **Remove** takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.
3. **Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer** is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.
4. Press **Save lead-time pricing**. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.

| What it touches | How |
| --- | --- |
| The rental charge | The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, "Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%". Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons |
| When it is worked out | When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. "From $X a day" stays at the base rate |
| When it is locked | On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage |
| Other discounts | The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it |
| Owner revenue and commissions | Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts |
| Staff | Change it on a booking under **More options** on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted |

> Tip: A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: **Vehicles** > the car > **Rates** > Lead-time pricing for this car.
## Vehicle class rules

Open **Settings**, then **Vehicle class rules**. How a new car''s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.

1. The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.
2. Press **Add a rule** or **Change**: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.
3. **Try a car** gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.
4. **Delete** removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.

> Tip: A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.

## Official ServiceOntario forms

The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher''s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. Each form shows "Mapping to check" (a draft is ready) or "Official PDF in use". Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.
2. Choose **Preview with**: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press **Download a filled preview** and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.
3. Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or "Signed here by hand, in ink"), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. **Earlier mappings** lists every save, with who and when; **Load** puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners > Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.
4. Press **Checked: use for owners**. Every owner''s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with **Record an official form signed in ink**. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.
5. A new version from ServiceOntario? Press **Upload the official fillable PDF**: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.

> Good to know: SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company''s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner''s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form''s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.

## Blind Spot rental agreement

We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental''s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars'' rental agreement and Blind Spot''s own. Blind Spot''s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.

1. Open **Settings** > **Forms**. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press **Upload Blind Spot''s PDF** and choose Blind Spot''s blank form (2 pages, A4).
2. Press **Download the filled sample**: a made-up booking on the form. **Sample billed to an insurer** also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.
3. On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars'' HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative''s signature instead of Sam''s.
4. Press **Checked: use for bookings**. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.
5. Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.
6. A new version of Blind Spot''s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for **Checked: use for bookings**, and bookings keep the version in use until then.

> Good to know: Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.

The renter''s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking''s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter''s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the "Your signed rental agreement" email. Admin > Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.

## Agreements to sign: investors and staff

Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person''s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).

1. Investor: open **People** > **Investors** and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press **Send the agreement to sign**. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press **Send to sign**.
2. Once the investor signs, the agreement shows **Awaiting countersignature** on the investor''s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press **Countersign**. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.
3. Staff: open **People** > **Team**. Under Staff agreements, press **Send the agreement to sign** beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.
4. A field staff member''s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.
5. They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.
6. Already sent or signed with old terms? Press **Send a new agreement** beside the person: it is filled with the current terms (for staff who live in Canada: Canada, CAD, Interac e-Transfer or direct deposit) and sent to sign the same way. The one waiting is withdrawn; a signed one stays on file, marked superseded, and keeps their portal open until they sign the new one. Someone in Canada still on the old terms (the Philippines, USD, OnlineJobs.ph) shows **Lives in Canada: needs the Canadian terms**, and a To do lists them.
7. Your own PDF instead? **Send a PDF to sign** still works.
8. Sent by mistake? Press **Withdraw** and give the reason.

## The user guides

**Settings** > **Guides**. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.

1. Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.
2. Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press **Show the preview** to see it as people will. Press **Save the draft**; each save is kept in the section''s history.
3. Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press **Add a chapter**. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.
4. Press **Publish version** (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.
5. The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.

## The guides keep up by themselves

After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.

1. Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.
2. The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal''s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.
3. Such a section says **Changed automatically on** and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide''s editor. Not right? Open the section and press **Revert**: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.
4. This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section''s history. There is nothing to review.
5. A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.

> Tip: The card "The guides keep up by themselves" at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.

## Insurers and the other lists

1. Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in **Money** > **Insurers**.
2. To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press **Add**.
3. Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.

## Promo codes: end dates and reminders

**Settings**, **Promo codes**.

- Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.
- A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.
- A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with "This code has expired".
- A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.
- The list shows each code''s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.

## Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage

**Settings** > **Card coverage** is the list renters see at `carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage` and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.

1. The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer''s own document, and when it was last checked.
2. Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press **Save**. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.
3. A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer''s own document unticked and the summary''s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer''s guide.
4. Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.

> Tip: A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer''s guide.

## Reviews: review requests and Google

**Settings** > **Reviews**: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.

1. When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.
2. The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile''s own review link.
3. Google Business Profile: press **Connect Google** and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.
4. A clear match stops that renter''s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press **Confirm**, **Not this renter** or **Match to a booking**.

> Tip: Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and "I already left a review", Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.

### Pair the card reader
**Settings** > **Card reader**. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open **Settings**, then **Generate pairing code**. Type the three words in **Pairing code**, name the reader (Front desk) and press **Pair reader**. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. **Remove** takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account''s statement descriptor.

### Rewards
**Settings** > **Rewards**. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter''s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.

1. **Ways to earn**: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend''s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows "Received reward points"), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter''s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).
2. **Tiers**: Gold from 1,000 points earned in 12 months, Platinum from 15,000, Black from 60,000 (below Gold a renter is a Member). Points earned count, so using points never lowers a tier. Press **Change** on a tier for its name and points. Tiers give perks, not discounts; tier codes issued before release 40 work until they end.
3. **Perks**: Instant Book (Gold), Any car, any time (Platinum) and a free rental day a year (Black). Each tier keeps the perks below it. **Change** a perk to move it to another tier, reword it or switch it off. **Change the response time** sets how fast Fleet answers an Any car request (4 hours); the open ones are listed with their answer-by time.
4. Points and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code, except the Black tier''s free day: CarmaCars pays for it, and the owner''s payout is worked out on the price before it.
4. **Google reviews claimed** lists every claim; **Reverse** takes the points back with a reason. **A renter''s points**: find the renter, then **Add or take off points** with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).
5. **Emails and notices to renters**: every Rewards email, each also a notice in the renter''s portal (a text only when they have no email): the welcome, points earned, a new tier, the free day, close to the next tier, points waiting, the 7-day reminder, the free day ending, the monthly statement and the birthday and holiday rewards. Each shows how many went in the last 30 days. **Preview** shows the email with sample values; **Turn off** stops it; **Change** sets the timings or switches them all off. Marketing ones carry an unsubscribe link and never go to someone who unsubscribed.
6. **Birthday and holiday rewards**: a percent off the rental charge by tier for a pickup near the renter''s birthday (7 days either side) or on a holiday weekend: Platinum 10%, Black 20%; Gold is off (0%) until you give it a percent. The bigger one applies, never both, never below the car''s lowest daily price, never on insurer or Owner Bookings. The request or offer keeps it. **Change** a tier for its percents or to switch it off; the holidays are listed with their next weekend: **Turn off**, **Remove** or **Add a holiday** by its date rule.

### Setup checklist
**Settings** shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars'' own accounts. **Add to Apple Wallet** stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker''s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.


Program: **Call and Text buttons go through Quo** (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device''s own phone and messages apps.

## Stuck? help

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Stuck? help**: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. **Where people get stuck**, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.

### API access (Claude and scripts)

Settings > **API access** connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring ("hire Ana as customer service"). **Connect from Claude**: in Claude, Settings > Connectors > Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press **Allow**. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, **Make a key**: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; **Revoke** stops it at once. The **Call log** lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.

### The logo

The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings > **Site settings**, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).

## Deposits stay as holds (release 28)

Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking''s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with **Re-authorize the hold**: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.

**Program settings**: **Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)** is on: Stripe approved it for the account. Every deposit hold (the pay link, the saved card, **Re-authorize the hold**, the reader) asks for a longer authorization, about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise; a card that cannot gets the standard hold by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in **Fees**, editable as every fee.

## Updated terms to accept

**Settings** > **Updated terms**. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with **Requires acceptance** on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.

1. Press **Publish a version**. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).
2. Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and **What changed**: people read this summary first.
3. Paste **The new text**. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site''s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site''s page.
4. Leave **Requires acceptance** on and press **Publish a version**.
5. Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees **We''ve updated our terms** full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.
6. **Accepted** on each version opens who accepted it and when.

> Good to know: It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.

> Good to know: Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.

### Card processing fee for a debit deposit
Program settings: **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)** and **Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)** (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.

## My profile and name changes (release 34)
Settings > **My profile** has your display name, **Request a name change** for your legal name, your phone number and **Change my password**. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.

## AI auto-replies (release 36)

**Settings** > **Program settings**, the AI auto-replies group, answers common questions by itself, only from the FAQ (**Site content**), within Workers AI''s free daily allowance. Each channel has its switch, on by default: texts to the CarmaCars number, emails to the inboxes listed (help@in.carmacars.ca), the website live chat, WhatsApp, Facebook Page messages and Instagram messages.

1. A question the FAQ answers gets the answer at once. A text asked between 1 am and 5 am is answered at 5 am (the quiet hours are settings).
2. When the FAQ does not answer it, or the model is not sure enough (70%), nothing is sent: a text stays in Messages for staff, and an email or a Meta message becomes a To do for customer service, **Answer** and the question.
3. Each person gets at most 5 automatic answers a day, never while a staff member texted them in the last 2 hours, and none once the day''s free AI allowance is used.
4. The card **AI auto-replies: the last answers** shows today''s answers and the last questions, with what was sent or why not.

Messenger, Instagram and WhatsApp need the Meta app''s webhook set to https://carmacars.ca/api/webhooks/meta with the verify token shown in the settings, and the Worker secrets META_APP_SECRET (and WHATSAPP_TOKEN with the WhatsApp number id). TikTok has no inbound message path for businesses, so it is not answered.

## Address suggestions (release 36)

The address fields suggest Canadian addresses from the site''s own address database (Statistics Canada''s Open Database of Addresses, loaded by the addresses workflow, Ontario first). Google is asked only for what the database does not have, and only when its key is set.

## Card coverage: the facts the booking check uses (release 35)

Each card also has: **Network** (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), **Includes rental car damage coverage (CDW)** (Yes, No or Unknown), **Vehicle types not covered** (comma separated: exotic, luxury, truck, van, off_road, antique, motorcycle, limousine, rv), **Must decline the rental company''s CDW** and **Must pay the full rental on the card**. A renter on card coverage picks their card from this list; the site checks it against the car''s value (the Black Book value or the estimate on the car), the car''s type and the length of the rental, and refuses a card that does not cover it. Unknown sends the renter to staff review. Exotic makes are listed in **Program** > **Coverage checks**.

## Fuel prices and delivery (release 35)

- **Program** > **Fuel and charging at the return**: the local pump prices of regular, premium and diesel (a litre), the multiplier (1.25), the refuelling fee ($20), the price a kWh for electric cars ($0.40), and the tank and battery sizes for a car without its own. Update the pump prices every week: **Today** reminds you after 7 days.
- **Airports and delivery** > **Delivery rate and origin**: the base fee each way ($75), the km it includes from the company''s location (15), the rate per km after them ($2), and the straight line to road distance factor (1.3) used when the maps service gives no road distance. A car whose rate card has its own delivery or pickup fee keeps it; every other car follows the base.

## Automatic answers and email budgets (release 36)

- Automatic answers: each channel (text, email, chat, social messages) switches on or off, with the quiet hours, the daily limit per person and how sure the answer must be. The last answers and the questions left for a person show in settings and under renter messages; a question it cannot answer becomes a To do. They stay inside the free daily AI allowance.
- Email budgets: Settings, Usage shows the real daily email capacity of all our sending services together (Cloudflare included), and when a service is not sending, why. Receipts, signed copies and staff messages always go.
- First photo: each listing chooses its first photo, the plain car, a car-show photo with a model, or a flyer with the live price; the flyer is made again when the price changes.
- Rewards: points for a photo with a review and for every rental after the first; every way to earn is on the renter''s Rewards page.

## Owner emails: trips and the week (release 41)

Owners are not emailed when a booking comes in, is confirmed or changes, because many bookings are cancelled (owner_new_booking, owner_booking_confirmed and owner_booking_changed are off, with their texts and notices). They are emailed when a trip is complete and the car is back (owner_trip_completed: the car, dates, days, distance driven if recorded and their share, which says it shows on the next statement while the booking''s revenue is hidden from them), and every Monday at about 9:00 Toronto time (owner_weekly_summary: per car, last week''s trips with their share, the confirmed bookings of the next 14 days with dates only, and the month so far, provisional), only when there was activity. Only bookings that count toward the owner''s revenue are used, never Owner Bookings or Turo trips. The Monday email has a switch in Program settings: **Weekly summary email to owners** (on by default).

## Call helper (release 43)

**Settings**, **Call helper**: what staff read inside the caller pop-up while on a call. A change shows on the next call.

1. **Greetings**: one for each kind of caller (a caller we do not know, a renter with a booking, a renter with no booking now, a lead, a car owner, a staff member). Press **Change** and type what to say. `{staff}` becomes the first name of the person on the phone, `{caller}` the caller''s first name, `{booking}` the booking number and `{car}` the car. A greeting that is off, or that needs a name we do not have, falls back to the one for a caller we do not know, which stays on.
2. **Situations**: one button each. **Add a situation** or **Change**: the name on the button, then the steps, one a line (3 to 6 is best, 8 at most). Write a link to a page as `[Bookings](/bookings)`: an Admin gets the Admin page and staff get their own. Words in "quotes" are shown as what to say. **Order** sets the place of the button; switch **On** off to hide one, or **Remove** it.
3. **Quick answers**: the question, the answer, and more search words staff might type.
4. **Numbers from the settings**: never type an amount, a number of days or a percentage. Write its word in braces from this list, for example `{late_grace}` or `{deposit_tiers}`: staff read today''s value from Program settings, Fee defaults and Deposit tiers, and it changes the day the setting does. A word in braces that is not in the list is refused when you save.

Every change is in the audit log with the words before and after.

## Texts and email by message type (release 48)
Program settings, **Texts and email by message type**, lists each message that can go by text with how many texts it sent in the last 30 days. Turn on **Email ready for production** once Amazon SES is out of its sandbox: then only the urgent messages keep their texts (the pickup details and codes, a late return, a failed payment, a declined deposit), and every other message goes by email, by text only when the person has no email address or their email bounced. Press **Change** on a row to send that message by email only, text only, or text and email (the person''s choice). The deposit link, sign-in codes, staff alerts and texts typed by staff always stay texts. While the switch is off nothing changes.

## Deposits by e-Transfer or cash, and tips

1. **Deposit by e-Transfer or cash: a multiple of the deposit** (on) and its multiplier (2): a $300 deposit is $600 by e-Transfer or cash. A debit or prepaid card keeps its own multiplier. An amount set on one booking wins.
2. **Tips** (on): the pay page, the receipt and the after-trip email offer 10, 15 or 20% or an amount; **the salesperson''s share** (5000: half, the rest to the handover).

## The tracker''s price and duplicate leads (release 48)

In **Settings** > **Program settings**:

- The tracker''s price. "GPS tracker product: what a vehicle owner pays for the tracker (0: free)": owners whose cars are listed with us get the tracker free. "GPS tracker product: the number the site says ("free for the first 100 pre-orders")": 100, the number every page shows. "GPS tracker product: how many pre-orders really get the tracker free. Never shown on the site": 250, the count that closes the free offer; no page shows it or how many are left. "GPS tracker product: the pre-order price once the free pre-orders are taken": $90. "GPS tracker product: the regular price after launch": $175, used once "Trackers can be installed" is on. "GPS tracker product: the install price": $150 once per car, paid by everyone, owners included. The tracker pages, the services module, llms.txt and the confirmation email all read these.
- "GPS tracker product: the monthly service price per car by number of cars": the monthly service everyone pays besides the tracker and the install, vehicle owners included. $25 a month per car for 1 or 2 cars, $20 for 3 to 9 and $15 for 10 or more.
- "GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist": the words beside "Join the waitlist" while "Trackers can be installed" is off.
- "Duplicate leads: join a new website form to the person''s open lead" and "Duplicate leads: how many days back the rule looks": whether a new website form joins the person''s open lead by itself, and how many days back it looks.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.</p><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-settings-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Settings page</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with <b class="gd-ui">Open site settings</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Program settings: every timing and policy value.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Forms: Blind Spot&#39;s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:33%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.4%;top:40.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:73.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:84.9%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company&#39;s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">My profile</b>: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole (&quot;Good morning, Abbas and Mahad&quot; on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change the greeting name</b>, type it and save.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-program-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Program settings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking&#39;s all-in price a day) and <b class="gd-ui">Approve a renter&#39;s extension at once when nothing needs a person</b> (on). A car&#39;s own switch is in Fleet, the car, <b class="gd-ui">Edit details</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Renters extend themselves</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month&#39;s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the defaults</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Shifts published by themselves (on): the shift template (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day from November 23, 2026), how many days ahead (14) and the first day they may be published for; a handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own. Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Change a value and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/program</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/admin-25-program-settings-desktop-d16b066c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:25.8%;top:22%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:27.8%;top:49%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-lead-time-pricing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Lead-time pricing</h2><p class="gd-p">A car booked at short notice costs a little more and one booked well ahead a little less. Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: Lead-time pricing is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The switch turns it on or off for every car (on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The table holds the tiers: when the pickup is that many hours away, the rental charge changes by that percentage. By default: under 24 hours +15%, 24 to 72 hours +10%, 3 to 13 days 0%, 14 days or more −5%. Type the hours and the percentage on each row (a minus for less); <b class="gd-ui">Add a tier</b> adds one, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one off. Each row shows what it does to a $500 rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Also adjust bookings billed to an insurer</b> is off by default: an insurer pays its own rate, never a short-notice premium.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save lead-time pricing</b>. New quotes and requests use it; bookings already made keep theirs.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">What it touches</th><th scope="col">How</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The rental charge</td><td>The percentage of the rental charge only, before tax: one line in the price, &quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;. Never the fees, the deposit or add-ons</td></tr><tr><td>When it is worked out</td><td>When the quote is made (the car page, the cars list once dates are chosen, the request), from that moment to the pickup on Toronto clocks. &quot;From $X a day&quot; stays at the base rate</td></tr><tr><td>When it is locked</td><td>On the request: the offer, a change of dates and the payment keep the same percentage</td></tr><tr><td>Other discounts</td><td>The non-refundable discount, a promo code and a staff discount are worked out on the rental charge from the rates, as before, and show beside it</td></tr><tr><td>Owner revenue and commissions</td><td>Count the rental charge after it, as they count the discounts</td></tr><tr><td>Staff</td><td>Change it on a booking under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b> on the review screen; a price typed by hand replaces it. Rentals added by hand, Owner Bookings and placeholders are not adjusted</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car can turn it off or have its own tiers: <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; the car &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> &gt; Lead-time pricing for this car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-vehicle-class-rules" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicle class rules</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle class rules</b>. How a new car&#39;s class is decided from its VIN: the first rule that matches wins.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table lists each rule: its rank, what the car must be (a make, and patterns for the model, the trim and the body), the class it gets, the class once the car is old enough, a note and whether it is on. The lowest rank that matches is used; a car that matches no rule is Standard.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rule</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>: a rank, at least one condition, the class, optionally the years old after which an older class applies, and a note (it is shown as the reason for the class). A pattern is not case sensitive: ^911 matches models that start with 911. A rule with no condition, a pattern that does not compile and an older class equal to the class are refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try a car</b> gives the class the rules decide for a year, make, model, trim and body, and why.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> removes a rule; switch it off instead to keep it. Every add, change and delete is in the audit log, with before and after.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A rule changes the cars entered from then on. A car already listed keeps its class until you change it on the car.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-official-serviceontario-forms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Official ServiceOntario forms</h2><p class="gd-p">The five official forms are loaded with a mapping to the owner, car, company and lender details. Each is the form exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it: only its empty text boxes are filled; its own text and layout are never changed. A form whose stored PDF is not the publisher&#39;s download (or your upload of it) gives owners the data sheet instead. Its checkboxes, drop-downs and signatures are done by hand at the counter, in ink. Until you check a form, owners get a data sheet with the values.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. Each form shows &quot;Mapping to check&quot; (a draft is ready) or &quot;Official PDF in use&quot;. Its notes say what the form is for and which boxes are left blank on purpose.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Preview with</b>: a sample car (made-up values) or one of the cars. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download a filled preview</b> and check each value against the form. The preview uses the mapping on screen, saved or not.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change a field if needed: What goes in it (or &quot;Signed here by hand, in ink&quot;), a Format (for example YYYY/MM/DD) and Only when. Write what you changed and press Save the mapping. <b class="gd-ui">Earlier mappings</b> lists every save, with who and when; <b class="gd-ui">Load</b> puts one back on screen to preview and save again. Fleet can map the forms too (Owners &gt; Government forms), but only an Admin uploads a form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for owners</b>. Every owner&#39;s form of that kind is filled again, except ones already signed or filed. Owners download it, print it and sign it in ink; record it with <b class="gd-ui">Record an official form signed in ink</b>. Each form not checked yet is also a line on To do with the same button and Preview it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A new version from ServiceOntario? Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload the official fillable PDF</b>: the fields of the same name keep their mapping.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>SR-LV-006 (registration), SR-LV-012 (two registrants), ON00453 (a company&#39;s RIN), 013-1155 and 013-0169 (the tax-exempt transfer into an owner&#39;s corporation). 013-1155 is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person. ON00453 is an Adobe form: it opens in Adobe Acrobat Reader. Each form&#39;s notes list what to tick or choose at the counter. A car gets only the forms its onboarding method needs: no form for a Transfer of a car owned outright or financed (the sign-back on the permit), 013-1155 and 013-0169 only for a Lease through a new Owner Corporation.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-blind-spot-rental-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Blind Spot rental agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">We rent under Blind Spot Car Rental&#39;s insurance, so every booking has two agreements: CarmaCars&#39; rental agreement and Blind Spot&#39;s own. Blind Spot&#39;s is filled in from the booking, the renter and the car, and the renter signs both with one signature. Its PDF is stored privately, never on the website.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Forms</b>. The Blind Spot Car Rental agreement card is first. Press <b class="gd-ui">Upload Blind Spot&#39;s PDF</b> and choose Blind Spot&#39;s blank form (2 pages, A4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Download the filled sample</b>: a made-up booking on the form. <b class="gd-ui">Sample billed to an insurer</b> also fills the claim number, the adjuster and the insurance company. Check every box.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the form the old address (top left and twice in box 15) is replaced by the mailing address of Site settings, box 1 by CarmaCars&#39; HST number (Program settings, Company HST number; blank until it is entered), and box 21 has the representative&#39;s signature instead of Sam&#39;s.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>. From then on each booking gets it when its rental agreement is made; a renter whose agreement is already open gets it the next time they open the signing page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Box 21: Ahmad is written in a script hand, as Blind Spot asked. To use a real signature instead, upload a PNG under Authorized company representative; Remove the image goes back to the written name. Full name is for the signature record page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A new version of Blind Spot&#39;s form? Upload it the same way: it waits for <b class="gd-ui">Checked: use for bookings</b>, and bookings keep the version in use until then.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each box is filled only when the booking has the value: the renter and their licence, the additional drivers, the car (plate, make and model, the fleet number as vehicle number), the pickup as time and date out, the due-back date and time, the kilometres allowed, the rate rows (days, weeks or months @ the rate = the amount; a rental counted by the day, such as 31 days at the monthly rate, shows its daily rate rounded to the cent, and box 14 says how the charge was made), the underage fee, the Protection Plan as CDW, winter tires, the subtotal, HST (13% of the subtotal), total and deposit, the deposit received and the day it was taken (before pickup, the amount due at pickup), and for a booking billed to an insurer the insurer, claim number and adjuster. Other charges, such as delivery, are listed in box 14. The boxes filled at check-in and check-out stay blank until then. The fuel gauges are covered and the level of the check-in report (fuel out) and the check-out report (fuel in) is written in words, blank with no reading.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s signature goes in boxes 16, 17 and 20 of the signed copy, with the day they signed beside box 20 and a signature record page. Each later version (as picked up, as returned, corrected) carries the same signature and day. Both agreements are in the booking&#39;s Drivers and documents tab, in the renter&#39;s Documents, and the signed Blind Spot agreement is attached to the &quot;Your signed rental agreement&quot; email. Admin &gt; Today lists the HST number, the upload and the check until they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-agreements-to-sign-investors-and-staff" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Agreements to sign: investors and staff</h2><p class="gd-p">Investment agreements and staff agreements are made from the person&#39;s record and signed in their own portal, with the e-signature (never on paper).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Investor: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and the investor. Under Investment agreement, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b>. Check the values it is filled with (amount, yearly percentage, dates, exemption) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send to sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Once the investor signs, the agreement shows <b class="gd-ui">Awaiting countersignature</b> on the investor&#39;s page and on To do. It is not countersigned automatically: check it and press <b class="gd-ui">Countersign</b>. CarmaCars is bound once it has countersigned and the funds clear.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Staff: open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b>. Under Staff agreements, press <b class="gd-ui">Send the agreement to sign</b> beside the person. Pay, schedule, hours and the other values start from the staff profile and the defaults of their function in Program settings; change any before sending. For Sales the Pay is Commission only: the agreement then has no rate, schedule or hours, and pays the commission of section 3.4.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field staff member&#39;s agreement prints the home address they entered themselves. Staff enter their home address at their first sign-in, before they sign, or in their profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">They get a notice, check the key values and sign in their portal in a few taps (their name is the signature, or they draw it). The signed copy is filed with their documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Already sent or signed with old terms? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send a new agreement</b> beside the person: it is filled with the current terms (for staff who live in Canada: Canada, CAD, Interac e-Transfer or direct deposit) and sent to sign the same way. The one waiting is withdrawn; a signed one stays on file, marked superseded, and keeps their portal open until they sign the new one. Someone in Canada still on the old terms (the Philippines, USD, OnlineJobs.ph) shows <b class="gd-ui">Lives in Canada: needs the Canadian terms</b>, and a To do lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Your own PDF instead? <b class="gd-ui">Send a PDF to sign</b> still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Sent by mistake? Press <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> and give the reason.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-user-guides" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The user guides</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Guides</b>. The guide of each portal, as people read it under Guide.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each guide shows its version, when it was published and whether there are unpublished changes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a guide and press a section. Change its text and press <b class="gd-ui">Show the preview</b> to see it as people will. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the draft</b>; each save is kept in the section&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Move a section with the arrows, hide it, or press <b class="gd-ui">Add a chapter</b>. Upload a screenshot under Screenshots and paste the line it gives you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish version</b> (the next number). The portals show the new version at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The stored PDF is printed again by the guides-pdf workflow. Until then the guide says the web guide has newer edits.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-guides-keep-up-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The guides keep up by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">After every update of the site that changes the portals, the guides are checked without anyone asking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every screenshot is taken again on the new version of the site. One whose screen changed replaces the old one in the guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The text of each section whose screen changed, or that names a button the portals no longer show, is rewritten from the portal&#39;s own labels and menu, checked, and published. The PDFs of those guides are printed again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Such a section says <b class="gd-ui">Changed automatically on</b> and the date, in the list of guides and in the guide&#39;s editor. Not right? Open the section and press <b class="gd-ui">Revert</b>: the text it replaced comes back, published at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">This includes sections you edited: the newest automatic text is published, and every earlier version stays in the section&#39;s history. There is nothing to review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A rewrite that does not pass the checks is asked again, more strictly. If it still does not pass, the screenshots and button names are updated, the rest of the text stays as it was, and the next run tries again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The card &quot;The guides keep up by themselves&quot; at the top of Guides lists the last runs: when, how many screenshots were replaced, how many sections were rewritten, and how many PDFs were printed.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-insurers-and-the-other-lists" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Insurers and the other lists</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Insurers. Each insurer on file opens to edit its billing contact, email, phone, address and notes. Its rates by car class are in <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Insurers</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To add one, fill in the Add form (Name, Billing contact, Billing email and the rest) and press <b class="gd-ui">Add</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Airports, Promo codes and Quick replies work the same way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-promo-codes-end-dates-and-reminders" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Promo codes: end dates and reminders</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Promo codes</b>.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Every code made for a person has an end date: a game prize 7 days, a come-back offer 30, a Live visitors code 3 and a code made for one renter 30 unless you set another. The first card of Promo codes holds the 30 days and the two reminders.</li><li>A code for everyone may have no end date: empty Valid until. The Add form starts with an end date 30 days ahead.</li><li>A code that ended is refused wherever it is typed (the request form, an offer, Add a rental, a booking edit) with &quot;This code has expired&quot;.</li><li>A person who has not used a code is reminded 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and by text as they chose, never once they used it, unsubscribed or the code ended, and never twice. A game code reminder always goes; a reminder of any other code needs their consent to offers.</li><li>The list shows each code&#39;s end date and the reminders sent. The card Codes sent to people lists game prizes, come-back offers and Live visitors codes the same way.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-which-credit-cards-include-rental-car-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: which credit cards include rental car coverage</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card coverage</b> is the list renters see at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/credit-card-rental-coverage</span> and staff see under Card coverage in their portal. It starts filled in with 48 Canadian and US cards, each checked on October 23, 2026.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The table shows each card: who pays first (Primary, Secondary, or not stated), the car value limit (MSRP), the longest rental, whether the numbers were read in the issuer&#39;s own document, and when it was last checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a card under Change a card, open its official guide, correct what changed and press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. Changing the facts without a date marks the card checked today; type a Last checked date to record another day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A card whose numbers come from a published summary has Read in the issuer&#39;s own document unticked and the summary&#39;s link under Where the numbers came from. The page shows it as Unverified. Tick it once you have read the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a card with the Add form; untick Shown to hide one. Changes reach the public page at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A card not checked for 6 months shows on Today until it is checked again. The page tells renters to confirm with their card issuer and says CarmaCars decides no claims: keep the list to facts from the issuer&#39;s guide.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-reviews-review-requests-and-google" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reviews: review requests and Google</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b>: when review requests go, the Google review link and the Google Business Profile connection. Review requests are on from the start.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When review requests go: the check-out (on or off, the shortest rental, hours after the pickup), the request (minutes after the check-out), the reminder (hours) and the final follow-up (days), the sending hours (9 am to 9 pm), and the hold while charges are open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The Google review link: the Google place id (Site settings) makes it, or paste the Business Profile&#39;s own review link.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Google Business Profile: press <b class="gd-ui">Connect Google</b> and sign in with rent@carmacars.ca, then allow access. Reviews are read every 6 hours and matched to renters by name within 30 days after their return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A clear match stops that renter&#39;s reminders at once. A possible match waits in Reviews: press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Not this renter</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Match to a booking</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Until Google approves the Business Profile API for the project, the status says so and nothing else changes: renters still get the review link, and &quot;I already left a review&quot;, Mark reviewed and on-site reviews still stop the messages.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Pair the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Card reader</b>. On the Stripe S700, swipe from the left edge, open <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Generate pairing code</b>. Type the three words in <b class="gd-ui">Pairing code</b>, name the reader (Front desk) and press <b class="gd-ui">Pair reader</b>. The first time, a Stripe Terminal location is made from the mailing address in Site settings: write it as street, city, province and postal code. <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a reader off the list. Card statements read 18122211 Canada Inc., the Stripe account&#39;s statement descriptor.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Rewards</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rewards</b>. CarmaCars Rewards is on: 1 point per dollar of the rental charge after discounts (never fees, add-ons, coverage, tax or the deposit), 100 points = $1, redeemed from 500 points as a code of the renter&#39;s own, valid 90 days. Points end 12 months after the last rental or redemption, with a reminder email 30 days before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ways to earn</b>: each on or off with its points. Referral (500 to the referrer, 250 to the friend, at the friend&#39;s first completed rental), a follow on Instagram, TikTok or Facebook (50 each, once, granted on the click from the Rewards page, since a follow cannot be checked; a platform shows only with its page in Site settings), a review on carmacars.ca (100, any rating; the review shows &quot;Received reward points&quot;), a Google review (100 a rental, any rating, on the renter&#39;s word: they press I posted my review and give the name on it; hidden until the Google review page is set here), a damage-free rental (200: no damage, claim, cleaning or smoking fee, back on time), the birthday (100) and the first rental (100).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tiers</b>: Gold from 1,000 points earned in 12 months, Platinum from 15,000, Black from 60,000 (below Gold a renter is a Member). Points earned count, so using points never lowers a tier. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> on a tier for its name and points. Tiers give perks, not discounts; tier codes issued before release 40 work until they end.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Perks</b>: Instant Book (Gold), Any car, any time (Platinum) and a free rental day a year (Black). Each tier keeps the perks below it. <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a perk to move it to another tier, reword it or switch it off. <b class="gd-ui">Change the response time</b> sets how fast Fleet answers an Any car request (4 hours); the open ones are listed with their answer-by time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Points and codes come off the rental charge only and reduce Owner Revenue like any promo code, except the Black tier&#39;s free day: CarmaCars pays for it, and the owner&#39;s payout is worked out on the price before it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Google reviews claimed</b> lists every claim; <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> takes the points back with a reason. <b class="gd-ui">A renter&#39;s points</b>: find the renter, then <b class="gd-ui">Add or take off points</b> with a reason, or reverse any entry (for example, referral fraud).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Emails and notices to renters</b>: every Rewards email, each also a notice in the renter&#39;s portal (a text only when they have no email): the welcome, points earned, a new tier, the free day, close to the next tier, points waiting, the 7-day reminder, the free day ending, the monthly statement and the birthday and holiday rewards. Each shows how many went in the last 30 days. <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b> shows the email with sample values; <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops it; <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> sets the timings or switches them all off. Marketing ones carry an unsubscribe link and never go to someone who unsubscribed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Birthday and holiday rewards</b>: a percent off the rental charge by tier for a pickup near the renter&#39;s birthday (7 days either side) or on a holiday weekend: Platinum 10%, Black 20%; Gold is off (0%) until you give it a percent. The bigger one applies, never both, never below the car&#39;s lowest daily price, never on insurer or Owner Bookings. The request or offer keeps it. <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> a tier for its percents or to switch it off; the holidays are listed with their next weekend: <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Add a holiday</b> by its date rule.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Setup checklist</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> shows what still needs a key from one of CarmaCars&#39; own accounts. <b class="gd-ui">Add to Apple Wallet</b> stays hidden until the Apple Pass Type ID certificate is added (WALLET_PASS_CERT, WALLET_PASS_KEY, WALLET_WWDR_CERT, WALLET_PASS_TYPE_ID and WALLET_TEAM_ID in the Worker&#39;s secrets); then it shows on every confirmed booking.</p><p class="gd-p">Program: <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> (on) makes every Call and Text button use the CarmaCars number in Quo (chapter Texts and calls). Off, they open the device&#39;s own phone and messages apps.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-stuck-help" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Stuck? help</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Stuck? help</b>: turn it on or off, the minutes on a page without a successful action (3), and the errors (3) before the box offers the guide and the Academy lesson. <b class="gd-ui">Where people get stuck</b>, on the same page, lists the pages it showed on most in the last 30 days, with how often the guide and the lesson were opened.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">API access (Claude and scripts)</h3><p class="gd-p">Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">API access</b> connects Claude so you (or Mahad) can run CarmaCars from a Claude chat: bookings, offers, payments, refunds, returns, cars, rates, listings, owners, invoices, staff and hiring (&quot;hire Ana as customer service&quot;). <b class="gd-ui">Connect from Claude</b>: in Claude, Settings &gt; Connectors &gt; Add custom connector, paste https://carmacars.ca/api/mcp, then sign in to CarmaCars and press <b class="gd-ui">Allow</b>. Every change is two steps: Claude first shows what will change (nothing is changed yet), and does it only when you agree. Keys and connections made with every scope got the Admin scopes in release 33; a key with fewer scopes keeps them. For Claude Code or a script, <b class="gd-ui">Make a key</b>: copy it at once, it is shown only once. Each key or connection acts as its Admin, with the scopes chosen; <b class="gd-ui">Revoke</b> stops it at once. The <b class="gd-ui">Call log</b> lists every call (the previews too) with the values before and after. The database checks each action exactly as the Admin screens do.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The logo</h3><p class="gd-p">The site, every portal, every email and the documents show the brand logo. To use another, upload it under Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site settings</b>, the Logo card (PNG or JPEG for emails and documents).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-deposits-stay-as-holds-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits stay as holds (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every deposit by card is a hold (an authorization) that stays with Stripe: it is never captured by itself, so nothing is paid out and nothing has to be refunded. Capture only what is owed, and release the rest from the booking. The booking&#39;s Security deposit panel shows Hold expires with the date Stripe gives. When a hold nears its expiry while the car is out or tickets can still come in, Finance gets a To do with <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b>: a new hold on the saved card, then the old one is released.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Extended deposit holds (up to about 30 days)</b> is on: Stripe approved it for the account. Every deposit hold (the pay link, the saved card, <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b>, the reader) asks for a longer authorization, about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise; a card that cannot gets the standard hold by itself. It never touches the rental payment. Capturing a deposit hold by itself is off. The heavy cleaning fee (an excessively dirty or smoked-in car) is $300 in <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>, editable as every fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-updated-terms-to-accept" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Updated terms to accept</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Updated terms</b>. When the terms of use, the privacy policy or an agreement template changes, publish the new version here; with <b class="gd-ui">Requires acceptance</b> on, each person it binds accepts it before using their portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Publish a version</b>. Choose the Document (the terms of use and the privacy policy bind everyone with a portal; each agreement binds the people who sign it: renters, owners, fleet suppliers, partners, investors, or staff and field).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Give the Version (for example the date it takes effect) and <b class="gd-ui">What changed</b>: people read this summary first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paste <b class="gd-ui">The new text</b>. For the terms of use or the privacy policy, leave it empty to use the site&#39;s current text; a text you paste also replaces the site&#39;s page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Leave <b class="gd-ui">Requires acceptance</b> on and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish a version</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Everyone it binds whose account was opened before sees <b class="gd-ui">We&#39;ve updated our terms</b> full screen on their next visit, with your summary and the text, and presses Accept. The acceptance is recorded with the time, the IP address, the device and the version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Accepted</b> on each version opens who accepted it and when.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It is a click-through acceptance of the new version: no signed agreement is voided and no renter signs the agreement of a past booking again. An Admin account is never asked.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every agreement is signed with the e-signature only (the identity steps, the IP address, the audit trail): a signature on paper is never recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form, which the government requires signed in ink, is recorded from its scan.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</h3><p class="gd-p">Program settings: <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit: percent (hundredths: 290 is 2.9%)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit: fixed part (cents)</b> (30 is $0.30). When a deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card, the renter pays this fee on it, as a separate non-refundable amount shown before they pay, on the receipt and on the Money tab. Set both to 0 to charge no fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-my-profile-and-name-changes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My profile and name changes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">My profile</b> has your display name, <b class="gd-ui">Request a name change</b> for your legal name, your phone number and <b class="gd-ui">Change my password</b>. When someone else asks to change the legal name on their agreements, it comes to To do with Approve and Decline, and shows on their page (owner, investor or renter). Approving changes the name on their account and record; agreements already signed keep the name they were signed with.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-ai-auto-replies-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">AI auto-replies (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>, the AI auto-replies group, answers common questions by itself, only from the FAQ (<b class="gd-ui">Site content</b>), within Workers AI&#39;s free daily allowance. Each channel has its switch, on by default: texts to the CarmaCars number, emails to the inboxes listed (help@in.carmacars.ca), the website live chat, WhatsApp, Facebook Page messages and Instagram messages.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A question the FAQ answers gets the answer at once. A text asked between 1 am and 5 am is answered at 5 am (the quiet hours are settings).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When the FAQ does not answer it, or the model is not sure enough (70%), nothing is sent: a text stays in Messages for staff, and an email or a Meta message becomes a To do for customer service, <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and the question.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each person gets at most 5 automatic answers a day, never while a staff member texted them in the last 2 hours, and none once the day&#39;s free AI allowance is used.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The card <b class="gd-ui">AI auto-replies: the last answers</b> shows today&#39;s answers and the last questions, with what was sent or why not.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Messenger, Instagram and WhatsApp need the Meta app&#39;s webhook set to https://carmacars.ca/api/webhooks/meta with the verify token shown in the settings, and the Worker secrets META_APP_SECRET (and WHATSAPP_TOKEN with the WhatsApp number id). TikTok has no inbound message path for businesses, so it is not answered.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-address-suggestions-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Address suggestions (release 36)</h2><p class="gd-p">The address fields suggest Canadian addresses from the site&#39;s own address database (Statistics Canada&#39;s Open Database of Addresses, loaded by the addresses workflow, Ontario first). Google is asked only for what the database does not have, and only when its key is set.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-card-coverage-the-facts-the-booking-check-uses-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card coverage: the facts the booking check uses (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Each card also has: <b class="gd-ui">Network</b> (Visa, Mastercard, American Express), <b class="gd-ui">Includes rental car damage coverage (CDW)</b> (Yes, No or Unknown), <b class="gd-ui">Vehicle types not covered</b> (comma separated: exotic, luxury, truck, van, off_road, antique, motorcycle, limousine, rv), <b class="gd-ui">Must decline the rental company&#39;s CDW</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Must pay the full rental on the card</b>. A renter on card coverage picks their card from this list; the site checks it against the car&#39;s value (the Black Book value or the estimate on the car), the car&#39;s type and the length of the rental, and refuses a card that does not cover it. Unknown sends the renter to staff review. Exotic makes are listed in <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Coverage checks</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-fuel-prices-and-delivery-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fuel prices and delivery (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Program</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Fuel and charging at the return</b>: the local pump prices of regular, premium and diesel (a litre), the multiplier (1.25), the refuelling fee ($20), the price a kWh for electric cars ($0.40), and the tank and battery sizes for a car without its own. Update the pump prices every week: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> reminds you after 7 days.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Airports and delivery</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Delivery rate and origin</b>: the base fee each way ($75), the km it includes from the company&#39;s location (15), the rate per km after them ($2), and the straight line to road distance factor (1.3) used when the maps service gives no road distance. A car whose rate card has its own delivery or pickup fee keeps it; every other car follows the base.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-automatic-answers-and-email-budgets-release-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Automatic answers and email budgets (release 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Automatic answers: each channel (text, email, chat, social messages) switches on or off, with the quiet hours, the daily limit per person and how sure the answer must be. The last answers and the questions left for a person show in settings and under renter messages; a question it cannot answer becomes a To do. They stay inside the free daily AI allowance.</li><li>Email budgets: Settings, Usage shows the real daily email capacity of all our sending services together (Cloudflare included), and when a service is not sending, why. Receipts, signed copies and staff messages always go.</li><li>First photo: each listing chooses its first photo, the plain car, a car-show photo with a model, or a flyer with the live price; the flyer is made again when the price changes.</li><li>Rewards: points for a photo with a review and for every rental after the first; every way to earn is on the renter&#39;s Rewards page.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-owner-emails-trips-and-the-week-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner emails: trips and the week (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">Owners are not emailed when a booking comes in, is confirmed or changes, because many bookings are cancelled (owner_new_booking, owner_booking_confirmed and owner_booking_changed are off, with their texts and notices). They are emailed when a trip is complete and the car is back (owner_trip_completed: the car, dates, days, distance driven if recorded and their share, which says it shows on the next statement while the booking&#39;s revenue is hidden from them), and every Monday at about 9:00 Toronto time (owner_weekly_summary: per car, last week&#39;s trips with their share, the confirmed bookings of the next 14 days with dates only, and the month so far, provisional), only when there was activity. Only bookings that count toward the owner&#39;s revenue are used, never Owner Bookings or Turo trips. The Monday email has a switch in Program settings: <b class="gd-ui">Weekly summary email to owners</b> (on by default).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call helper (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b>: what staff read inside the caller pop-up while on a call. A change shows on the next call.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Greetings</b>: one for each kind of caller (a caller we do not know, a renter with a booking, a renter with no booking now, a lead, a car owner, a staff member). Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> and type what to say. <span class="gd-url">{staff}</span> becomes the first name of the person on the phone, <span class="gd-url">{caller}</span> the caller&#39;s first name, <span class="gd-url">{booking}</span> the booking number and <span class="gd-url">{car}</span> the car. A greeting that is off, or that needs a name we do not have, falls back to the one for a caller we do not know, which stays on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Situations</b>: one button each. <b class="gd-ui">Add a situation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>: the name on the button, then the steps, one a line (3 to 6 is best, 8 at most). Write a link to a page as <span class="gd-url">[Bookings](/bookings)</span>: an Admin gets the Admin page and staff get their own. Words in &quot;quotes&quot; are shown as what to say. <b class="gd-ui">Order</b> sets the place of the button; switch <b class="gd-ui">On</b> off to hide one, or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Quick answers</b>: the question, the answer, and more search words staff might type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Numbers from the settings</b>: never type an amount, a number of days or a percentage. Write its word in braces from this list, for example <span class="gd-url">{late_grace}</span> or <span class="gd-url">{deposit_tiers}</span>: staff read today&#39;s value from Program settings, Fee defaults and Deposit tiers, and it changes the day the setting does. A word in braces that is not in the list is refused when you save.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Every change is in the audit log with the words before and after.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-texts-and-email-by-message-type-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Texts and email by message type (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Texts and email by message type</b>, lists each message that can go by text with how many texts it sent in the last 30 days. Turn on <b class="gd-ui">Email ready for production</b> once Amazon SES is out of its sandbox: then only the urgent messages keep their texts (the pickup details and codes, a late return, a failed payment, a declined deposit), and every other message goes by email, by text only when the person has no email address or their email bounced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> on a row to send that message by email only, text only, or text and email (the person&#39;s choice). The deposit link, sign-in codes, staff alerts and texts typed by staff always stay texts. While the switch is off nothing changes.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-deposits-by-e-transfer-or-cash-and-tips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Deposits by e-Transfer or cash, and tips</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Deposit by e-Transfer or cash: a multiple of the deposit</b> (on) and its multiplier (2): a $300 deposit is $600 by e-Transfer or cash. A debit or prepaid card keeps its own multiplier. An amount set on one booking wins.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Tips</b> (on): the pay page, the receipt and the after-trip email offer 10, 15 or 20% or an amount; <b class="gd-ui">the salesperson&#39;s share</b> (5000: half, the rest to the handover).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="settings-the-tracker-s-price-and-duplicate-leads-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The tracker&#39;s price and duplicate leads (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b>:</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The tracker&#39;s price. &quot;GPS tracker product: what a vehicle owner pays for the tracker (0: free)&quot;: owners whose cars are listed with us get the tracker free. &quot;GPS tracker product: the number the site says (&quot;free for the first 100 pre-orders&quot;)&quot;: 100, the number every page shows. &quot;GPS tracker product: how many pre-orders really get the tracker free. Never shown on the site&quot;: 250, the count that closes the free offer; no page shows it or how many are left. &quot;GPS tracker product: the pre-order price once the free pre-orders are taken&quot;: $90. &quot;GPS tracker product: the regular price after launch&quot;: $175, used once &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is on. &quot;GPS tracker product: the install price&quot;: $150 once per car, paid by everyone, owners included. The tracker pages, the services module, llms.txt and the confirmation email all read these.</li><li>&quot;GPS tracker product: the monthly service price per car by number of cars&quot;: the monthly service everyone pays besides the tracker and the install, vehicle owners included. $25 a month per car for 1 or 2 cars, $20 for 3 to 9 and $15 for 10 or more.</li><li>&quot;GPS tracker product: the words beside Join the waitlist&quot;: the words beside &quot;Join the waitlist&quot; while &quot;Trackers can be installed&quot; is off.</li><li>&quot;Duplicate leads: join a new website form to the person&#39;s open lead&quot; and &quot;Duplicate leads: how many days back the rule looks&quot;: whether a new website form joins the person&#39;s open lead by itself, and how many days back it looks.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('va', 'fleet', 'chapter', 'finance', 'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site. The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.

## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.', 'Fleet', 'Field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews, similar cars and listings.',
  'You keep the cars moving: field jobs, daily checks, photo reviews after returns, and the listings with their duplicate check and plate covering. There is no commission for Fleet, but your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.

Your rail: Queue, Today, Field jobs, Field hours, Daily checks, Photo reviews, Calendar, Listings, Similar cars, Find a renter and Scorecard.

## Schedule field jobs

Every confirmed booking gets its handover (or delivery) and return (or pickup) jobs by itself, at the booking''s times and place, and put on a shift: the shift covering its time, or that day''s (see Shifts and who gets a job). The people on the shift share its jobs, least busy first. You check and change them.

1. Jobs, next three days: each with its place, its shift, its field staff and whether they acknowledged it. "Made from the booking" marks the ones made by themselves; when the booking moves, they move too, unless you changed them.
2. Change a job with **To a shift** (another shift), **Assign** or **Reassign** (a field person on a shift that day when the day has shifts, or an Admin), **Move** (time and place) or **Cancel**.
3. Handovers and returns without a job (when the automatic jobs are off, or one was cancelled) are listed first: press **Schedule**, the place filled in from the booking.
4. An Admin turns the automatic jobs or the assignment off in Settings > Program.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-02-field-jobs-desktop-8e721230.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 565; address: carmacars.ca/va/fleet; pins: 1 17.9 51.3")

## Shifts and who gets a job

Field staff take their shifts from the schedule published by itself: every hour, up to 14 days ahead, from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day), only forward from the latest shift already published. A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own (90 minutes either side). A job is given by itself only to a field person who passed the academy and holds a shift that day, and work lands only on days with shifts.

1. On **Field jobs**, **Shifts, next seven days** shows each day and how many people are on a shift, and each shift its jobs (**Jobs on it**). A shift with jobs and nobody on it is marked; within 24 hours of its start you get an alert and a To do, once.
2. Need more? Press **Publish shifts**: the first day''s start and end, how many people, and for how many days the same hours repeat. A shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them on their phones.
3. **Add a person** puts someone on a shift and **Remove** takes them off. A person who has not passed the academy cannot take shifts or be given a job.
4. A shift nobody claimed keeps its jobs: field staff see them when they look for shifts to claim, and the one who claims it gets them. A shift given up or swapped takes its jobs along; a cancelled shift sends them to another shift.
5. Work due on a day with no shifts moves to the day before when it is known in advance, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day. The job shows its planned day and keeps the booking''s real time; the renter''s times never change. A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning: cover it, or move the booking time.
6. **Unassign** takes a job off its person and its shift; tick **Tell them** only if they should know. The Admins can be given a job too (no shift needed).

## Missing check-ins and check-outs

1. **Missing check-in and check-out** on Field jobs lists every past rental without its photos and readings (odometer, fuel, damage photos), closed bookings included.
2. Press **Give to field staff** and choose the person: they add the photos and readings from their Today page.

## Fleet map

At the top of **Field jobs**: every car on the map with its renter, booking, due-back time and state, the alerts, and the trips by booking, the same as the Admin''s. Every staff member sees the cars'' positions: customer service, Sales and Finance open the same map from **Find a car** (**Car map**), read only, and field staff under **Map**. Every car page and booking page shows **Where the car is**: moving or parked, when it last reported and **Open on the map**, or **No tracker yet**. Only Admins and fleet staff press **Seen** on an alert. Each owner sees where their own cars are, never the renter or the booking.

1. Press a car for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery and the trip under way.
2. An alert (speeding, left Ontario or the zone, still driving after the return time, low or unplugged tracker, not reporting) also comes to your bell and as an urgent phone alert. Call the renter, then press **Seen**.
3. A car still driving after its return time: call, send the late notice and offer a paid extension, as for any late return.

## Field hours

Field staff clock in and out on their phones. You see who is clocked in and every shift of the two-week pay period, and you fix what they cannot.

1. Open **Field hours**. **Clocked in now** lists who is on, since when. **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between pay periods.
2. Someone forgot to clock out: press **Clock out for them**, set the time they finished and write the reason.
3. Someone forgot to clock in, or a time is wrong: **Add hours** enters a shift, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason; the change is kept in a log with what it was before.
4. Once an Admin approves the pay run of a period, its shifts are locked: ask the Admin. You see hours only, not rates or pay.

### Where they clocked in
The hours list shows where each person clocked in and out: a map link and the distance from the lot. A clock in or out over 500 m away, or with the location refused, is shown in bold with the reason the person wrote. Their location is asked only at those two moments, never in between.

## Daily checks

Twice a day: the opening check by 9:00 and the closing check by 18:00.

1. Open **Daily checks** and choose **Opening check** or **Closing check**.
2. Each line shows what was found. Tick OK, or Problem with a note.
3. Press **Save the opening check** (or **Save the closing check**). You can save it again.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-03-daily-checks-desktop-be06d6c0.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 820; address: carmacars.ca/va/checks; pins: 1 6.5 15.4, 2 44.7 42.0, 3 64.2 94.0")

## Check a car out or in

Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in from the booking.

1. On a confirmed booking press **Check in (pickup)**; on a booking on rent, **Check out (return)**. Today lists the ones due, each with its button.
2. The checklist field staff use opens: readings (km and fuel or charge), the photo set with the plate and the gauges, damage close-ups and both signatures.
3. Afterwards press **Photo report**: times, Late by, kilometres, fuel, photos and the return charges. Fleet waives a charge with **Waive** and a reason.

## Photo reviews after a return

After each return, the field photo set waits under **Photo reviews**. Compare it with the pickup set. Press **Review done**, or **Ask for a re-shoot** if a photo is missing or unclear.

## Similar cars

A possible duplicate never keeps a car off the site: it shows on the car''s checklist until you decide. Only Same car takes it off.

1. Each flag shows the car, what it looks like (same VIN, plate, photo or specs) and the other car.
2. Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.
3. Press **Not a duplicate** with a note when they are different cars, or **Same car** when they are.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 460; address: carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars; pins: 1 23.6 30.4, 3 94.8 30.4")

## Rates and kilometres

From a listing, press **The car and its rates**, or open the car from Field jobs and its **Rates & fees** tab.

1. Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.
2. Keep **Use the defaults** for the kilometres, or choose **Custom for this car**.
3. Check What renters pay under the fields, then press **Save the rates**. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.
4. **Price limits**, below: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts, read only. Offers, promo codes and lead-time pricing stay between them; an Admin or the owner changes them, and only an Admin allows one booking outside them.

## Listings and covering plates

1. Open **Listings**. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.
2. The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.

![](/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 340; address: carmacars.ca/va/listings; pins: 1 54.5 49.1")

3. The listing''s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plates are checked by themselves: a plate found is blurred (Covered automatically), a photo with none is marked No plate visible, and a photo the check is not sure of stays Plate not checked. **Undo** on a photo takes an automatic decision back. To cover one yourself, press **Cover the plate**: the editor opens under the photo; **Suggest the plate** asks for the box. A photo filed under the wrong shot: **Remove** under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.
4. Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.
5. Only a plate that is there is blurred, tight to the plate with a soft edge, so no character can be read (nothing is drawn on it; a car with no front plate gets no box there), then **Save the covered photo**.
6. No plate in the shot? **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg "phone; size: 390 776; pins: 3 52.6 78.9, 4 50.0 43.8, 5 61.5 62.1, 6 43.1 92.3")

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.

## Missing angles and short videos

On a listing, below First photo (Sales: in the Marketplace kit of the car).

1. A required angle with no photo? Fleet and Sales press **Make** and the angle (for example **Make Rear**): the image model makes the view from the car''s photos, within its free daily use. Check it is the same car, then **Approve** or **Reject**.
2. Press **Make a short video** for a 9:16 video of the car''s approved photos with the price and the call to action. Keep the tab in front until it says Saved, then **Download** it or schedule it on your Marketing page (Scheduled posts).

> Watch out: An AI view shows on the site after the real photos, labelled AI view. It is never the cover and never damage or condition evidence. A real photo always replaces it.

## Publish now

Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.

1. Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press **Publish now**. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).
2. What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.
3. New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.

> Tip: A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.

## Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms

**Cars** > **Calendar sync**: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.

1. Turo has no calendar link: Turo''s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.
2. An email the reader cannot place waits as "Which car is this?": press **Which car is this?** and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car''s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: **Add as a Turo trip** (choose the car, check the dates) or **Dismiss**. A trip whose email did not come: **Add a Turo trip** on the car.
3. Each Turo trip shows the guest''s name and phone when Turo''s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.
4. Turo cannot read our calendar: under "Block on Turo", block each CarmaCars booking on the car''s Turo calendar, then press **Done on Turo**. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.
5. Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open **Add a calendar link**, choose the platform, paste it and press **Add the link**. Copy the car''s CarmaCars link for that platform with **Copy** and paste it into the platform''s calendar import.
6. A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.

### Add the photos and readings
A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. Open the booking and press **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings**: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter''s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.

## Bookings now

**Rentals** > **Bookings** opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as **Out (pickup not recorded)** left without a check-in: press **Mark picked up**, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. A car overdue or due back today has **Returned** (here, on Today and at the top of the booking): give the return time (now, or earlier; lateness follows it) and the km and fuel if known. The overdue messages stop and the task for the photos is yours. The search above it finds any booking.

### The renter says the car is back

An urgent To do "The renter says the car is back" means the renter pressed **I''ve returned the car** on an overdue booking. Their overdue notices are paused. Open the booking, check the car (place, tracker, the renter''s photos), then press **Confirm** (correct the odometer, fuel or time first if needed; the trip is completed) or **Deny** with the reason (the renter is told and the notices start again).

**Start a listing** takes the VIN from the car: **Scan the barcode** in the door frame or under the windshield, or **Photo of the VIN**.

**Add photos** on a listing takes any number of photos at once, in any order: each is sorted to its shot. A photo that fits no shot goes in with **Extra outside photos** or **Extra inside and detail photos**; drag the extras into their order in the review and press **Save the order**. 10 photos and one outside photo complete the listing. Outside photos are framed big on the studio floor with a shadow under the tyres; a watermark or caption at a photo''s edge is cut off by itself. **Cover the plate** opens with the plate box suggested: check it and save. A car small in the frame, or no model name behind it: press **Frame the outside photos again** (then check the plates again). A bad cut-out (a mirror missing, background left): press **Edit the cut-out**, erase or restore with the brush, move or size the car on the studio, then **Save as a new version**. The version before is kept; if the car did not move, the plate check carries over. Every photo gets a light touch-up by itself; tick **Use original colours** under a photo to make it again without it. Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom: a real photographed dealership room when one is stored (the car about 70% of the width, its wheels on the floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection; no logo on a real wall), else the dark drawn showroom (the logo on the wall, the model''s name behind the car on the cover). A cut-out that is not clean enough is never placed in a room: the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual), noted on the photo. A car still on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car**; **Listings** > **Apply showroom to every car** does every car. Under a photo, **Redo** makes it again and **Back to the original** puts back the version before. **Marketing photos** on a listing makes copies in other scenes for Marketplace and social posts (choose a scene or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, then **Make the marketing set**); the website''s photos stay as they are. **First photo** on a listing chooses what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit: **Plain car**, **With a model** (the image model''s car-show photo, a fully clothed adult model beside the car) or **Flyer** (the price a day from the live rates, the call to action and the logo on the cover). Switch any time; until the chosen one is made the plain cover shows.
## One screen, many photos (release 28)

**Import photos from a Google Drive link** on a listing adds the photos of a public Drive folder to the car, sorted and processed like Add photos. **Listings** > **Import photos from Drive** reads a whole folder of folders (one per make, then per car), proposes the car for each folder, and imports once you confirm the table. The page follows the import and ends with what was imported, skipped and failed, and why. The same Drive file is never added twice. Customer service can import into a car whose listing is already started; Fleet and Admin can start one.

Check-in and check-out are one screen on the booking page: the time, km, fuel, many photos at once (tag angles if you like) and a note. The renter''s own photos join the same report; each photo shows who took it. On a car''s page, record **Pickup from owner** and **Return to owner** with photos: the owner sees them.

## Repair costs on a car

On a car''s page, **Kickbacks and repairs** lists its repair costs and the kickbacks partners paid on it. **Add a repair cost**: the date, the shop or another vendor, what was done, the amount and tax, who paid (CarmaCars, the owner or the insurer), the claim and a photo or PDF of the receipt.

## When a check stops the pickup or the return (release 33)
On the booking page, **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) lists each check that stops it, in plain words. When the trip must go ahead anyway, press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return), give the actual time, the km and fuel if you know them, and why. An Admin gets an alert and approves in one tap; the pickup (or the return) is then recorded with the time you entered, and the booking''s history says who asked and who approved. You can cancel your request while it waits. A trip that happened and was never recorded: **Ask to record a past trip** with both times; once an Admin approves, the booking lands in Returned so the deposit can be settled.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars**, then **Incident cards**, prints the card for the visor or the glovebox: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, our support and roadside numbers, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. On a car''s page, **Incident card** prints that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints every car, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks. Laminate it and put one in each car. The insurance policy on the card is set by an Admin; until it is, the card tells the renter to ask for the slip. No price is ever printed on it.

## Government forms (release 35)
The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change.

## Odometer and fuel at every check-in and check-out

Every check-in and check-out on one screen asks for two photos besides the others:

1. **Photo of the dashboard**: the odometer and the fuel gauge, from the camera roll or the camera. The site reads it and asks, for example, "Odometer 45,210 km, fuel 3/4: correct?". Press **Yes, correct**, or **No, I will type it** and type the odometer and pick the fuel in eighths.
2. **Selfie in front of the car**: taken now with the camera, never from the camera roll. A selfie without a fresh capture time is noted on the report for you to check; it never stops the check-in.

At the return the site compares with the pickup: km driven, km over the included allowance and the fuel difference. The extra km (the booking''s rate per km) are added to the booking by themselves. The fuel is prepared as a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the local pump price of its grade x 1.25, plus the $20 refuelling fee (an electric car: battery kWh x the charge missing x $0.40, plus the fee). You and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; no card is charged by it. The photo report shows both dashboard photos side by side with the readings and these charges.

## Change the car of a confirmed booking

A car with a problem before pickup? On the booking, press **Change the car**, choose a car free for the dates and say why. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet; more to pay is left open for the renter, less becomes a refund for approval. The jobs move to the new car and the renter gets one email.

## An accident reported by a renter

A renter can report an accident from the accident card on their booking. It opens the incident with its first-response steps and your To do, and sends you an urgent alert (on duty) and to Admins: what happened, where, the photos and videos, the other party, the police report number, whether anyone is hurt and whether the car can be driven. Call the renter at once; a car that cannot be driven is already out of service with its calendar blocked.
## Payments and calls (release 35)
Fleet takes payments on a booking''s **Money** tab: text or email a pay link, charge the saved card when the renter agreed, hold the deposit, or record cash or an e-Transfer received (within your single limit; Finance gets a To do to check it). Refunds, captures and voids stay with Finance and the Admins.

Calls and texts about pickups, returns, deliveries and cars on rent come to Fleet first: the caller pop-up shows them, and **More fleet** > **Calls and texts** is your inbox. A car late back has **Returning now** on its late panel: press it when the renter says they are on the way, and they get no more overdue reminders for that return time.

The official ServiceOntario forms of each owner''s car are on the owner''s page and the car''s page, under **Government forms**. Open a form, press **Change a value**, choose the box, type the value and the reason, and **Save**: the form is made again as a new version, and the earlier versions stay under **Versions** with their downloads. **Back to the records** undoes a change. A form signed in ink or filed is never changed. **Make again** keeps the values changed by hand unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. **Owners**, then **Government forms**, opens the forms'' mapping (which value goes in which box): preview it on a sample car, write what you changed and save; every save is kept under **Earlier mappings**. Only the boxes are filled: the form''s own text and layout never change. The owner signs each form on screen: the page shows **Owner''s signature** beside the form (who, when, the version) and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature on it. A value changed after signing shows **Changed since signed** and the owner is asked to sign again.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Field jobs** > **Close ended trips**: tick the trips that ended and were never closed, mark them returned on time or late (with the time), choose the deposit decision (deduct the balance owed, deduct the late fee, or release in full) and press **Close**. An expired card hold is settled by expiry at once. An Admin presses Release for the rest. On a booking, an expired hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## The primary photo (release 43)

The first photo of a car is always its front exterior. When a car shows the flag **Primary photo is not exterior** on the Vehicles list, its best outside photo is not on the site yet: add or approve one. **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every photo of the car again from its original with Gemini (the background replaced by the showroom, inside photos cleaned up and sharp, a plate blurred only where the car has one, tight to the plate) and generates the angles the car has no photo of, marked **AI generated**. A photo the check refuses three times stays off the site, flagged. Fleet also has the **Photo standard** card on Listings: each car''s photos at the standard, AI angles, flagged photos and last run, with **Redo this car now** and **Redo every car**. The whole fleet is brought to the standard by itself every 5 minutes, newest listed cars first.

## Field applicant calls (release 35)

Field applicants who pass the AI interview book a 10-minute interview date in the hour before the weekly townhall. **Field applicant calls** on your home page lists the six slots and who took each one.

## Value and fuel on the car page (release 35)

**Cars** > the car > **Overview** > **Value and fuel**:

- **Canadian Black Book value** (with the date checked) or an **Estimated value (when no Black Book)**: renters on credit card coverage are checked against it. With neither, they go to staff review.
- **Tank (litres)** and **Fuel grade** (regular, premium or diesel; empty uses the class), or **Battery (kWh)** for an electric car. Empty uses the default in Program settings.

Press **Save**. Customer service sees the card; only Fleet and an Admin change it.

## Shifts, delivery and fuel (release 35)

- The shift board shows each field person''s availability, the standing weekly shifts, who is under the minimum, and for each slot the people to ask. A shift nobody claimed 48 hours ahead alerts you.
- You can approve new staff at the fourth onboarding step, or reject with a reason.
- Delivery is priced by distance from 1570 Midland Ave; the fuel line at the return is a suggestion from the tank and the pump price for you to check on the deposit review.
- An Admin can delete a car that has only test bookings; a car with a real booking stays.

## Calls first, texts after (release 37)

Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.

1. Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.
2. **Call before you text.** On a lead, a renter or a booking, **Call** is the first button and **Text** the second.
3. A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.
4. On your To do and on **Unanswered**, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.

## A lead you handle on a call (release 37)

When you answer or place a call with a lead, add a note on it, or create it from a call, the lead is yours for a limited time (15 minutes, as a Sales claim; an Admin can change it in **Settings** > **Sales**). Every call you handle adds the time again.

- Sales see **Being handled by** your first name and your function with the time, on the lead and in every list. They cannot claim it, call, text or email it, or set an outcome meanwhile, and **Next lead** skips it.
- Another customer service or Fleet person can still work it; their call or note takes the hold over.
- When it ends, the lead goes back to the salesperson who had a claim on it or who brought it, else to the open list. An Admin can **Release hold** earlier.
- A booking made from the lead is credited as always: customer service and Fleet get no sales commission for it.
- Nobody who has not finished onboarding holds a lead.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

## Every view generated from the car''s photos (release 47)

Every car now shows nine views generated by Gemini (front three-quarter first, then front, side, rear three-quarter, rear, dashboard, front seats, rear seats, trunk), made from the car''s own photos, the sample view of the angle, the stock photo of the model and the showroom background. A car with too few photos uses its check-in and check-out photos as references (never shown on the site). A view the check refuses three times is flagged and the car''s real photo of that angle stays on the site. The real photos stay on the car''s record. On **Photo standard**, **Generated set** shows each car''s views made out of nine; **Redo this car now** makes them again.

## Picked up, deposit pending (release 48)
When the renter cannot place the deposit hold at the pickup (the card is declined, the bank wants a call) and the car must go, you can let it go with the deposit owed. On the job, under the deposit line, open **Let the car go with the deposit owed**, say why, and go on with the check-in. On a booking, **Record the pickup now** has the box **Deposit not taken yet: let the car go owing it, because**, and the check-in panel has **Deposit not taken: let the car go owing it**. The booking then shows **Deposit pending $X** everywhere. Each morning the renter''s saved card is tried once; if that fails, the renter gets the deposit link by text (or email). After 48 hours an Admin gets a To do. You do nothing more: once the deposit is taken the chip changes by itself.

## Studio renders (release 48)

- Every car''s first photos are studio renders made from its own photos, the side profile first. Its real photos come after them.
- Renders go live by themselves. You get "Studio photos live" in your next digest: check the colour, wheels and trim, and that the side profile faces left.
- Something is off: open the car, **Studio photos**, then **Make again** or **Take off the site**.
- To render every published car now: **Listings**, **Photo standard**, **Render every published car**.

## Evidence for every fee (release 48)

Every fee is charged only with its evidence. On a booking''s Money tab, **Evidence for every fee** lists each fee with what it needs, what was found by itself and what is missing.

1. A fee that Needs evidence has a To do in the Fleet queue (titled "Field:" when the field staff capture it) saying exactly what to take: the guided cleanliness photos and description, a damage close-up, photos of where the car was left, a receipt.
2. Press **Attach evidence** on the line, choose what it is and add the photo or PDF (or a note). It is checked again at once; the To do closes by itself.
3. The return checklist does not complete a return that is not clean without 3 guided photos and a description. The smoking or cleaning fee it drafts waits for your review of the return, then Finance.
4. **Add a return charge**: non-return, improper return, theft recovery, a flat tire or a roadside call-out (cost plus $50; not for a mechanical fault that is not the renter''s). Add each actual cost with its receipt.

## Tracker events and pound flags (release 48)

On the **Fleet map**, below the map and the alerts. It shows once an Admin has turned Tracker events on.

**Tracker events** lists each event with its evidence: when, the car and booking, the speed and the map point, the charge and the clause, and who was told. One event per car, kind and 30 minutes. The renter and the car''s owner are told by themselves; you do not need to message them about the event itself.

- A speeding record over 180, 220 or 300 km/h carries one charge, at the highest limit reached in the event. An Admin or Finance presses **Charge**; you do not.
- Harsh driving and a speed over the alert level are a heads-up only.
- A Tracker unplugged or tampered with, or a car outside Ontario: call the renter.

**A car that leaves Ontario or Canada**: you get an alert, an email and a text at once. Call the renter. For Canada there is an urgent To do: leaving Canada needs written approval, so with no approval and no answer, tell an Admin.

**Pound flags**: a car parked at a known pound.

1. You get an urgent To do and alert. Open **Pound flags**: the lot''s phone and hours are on the row.
2. Call the lot to confirm the car is there and what releases it. Call the renter. Keep every receipt.
3. Press **Record the path** and choose: the non-return charge with the costs, the theft recovery charge with the costs (add the police report number), **Recovered, nothing to charge**, or **Not a pound**. Write what happened in a sentence.

> Tip: Not sure which charge applies? Non-return is for a car not back after the final late notice. Theft recovery is for a car stolen, or recovered by the police or a repossession. Ask an Admin when it is neither.

**Pound lots** are listed below, read only. Tell an Admin when a lot''s phone or hours are wrong, or a pound is missing.
